\par\par \b \uc2 DJ ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,668 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juni 2013\par 02:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--The following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range Larger Range \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 USD/CNY 6.1210-6.1300 6.1018-6.1500\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD 29.910-30.000 29.730-30.080 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    USD/KRW  1,133-1,140    1,130-1,144 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/SGD 1.2600-1.2635 1.2566-1.2700\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/MYR 3.1500-3.1700 3.1300-3.1800 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    USD/THB  30.50-30.92    30.44-31.00 \par    USD/PHP  43.00-43.32    42.60-43.59 \par    USD/IDR  9,900-9,950    9,810-10,000 \par    USD/INR  58.50-58.98    58.00-60.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis - Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/CNY - consolidation. The PBOC central parity rate may rise again Wednesday, possibly toward CNY6.1680, in tandem with the overnight USD/JPY rally. Onshore spot USD/CNY could hence be supportive as the onshore funding shortage eases amid talk that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has the tools such as the reverse repo, and even the ability to slash the reserve requirement ratio if needed, to help banks address their cash funding problems. The dollar's direction Wednesday will depend on what U.S. Federal Reserve chairman Bernanke says at the conclusion of the FOMC meeting tonight. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.1210 (June 3 record low), then at 6.1200 (psychological support), before 6.1018 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 6.1300 (psychological resistance), then at 6.1500 (psychological resistance), before 6.1700 (top of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/TWD - consolidation. More sideways price action is likely in USD/TWD, at least until tonight's U.S. FOMC outcome provides direction for the greenback. The pair may range within a 29.910-30.080 band demarcated by the 20-day Bollinger mid support and the entrance to the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. If USD/TWD ends the day below the 20-day Bollinger mid, the next target could be the Ichimoku Cloud support at 29.730. If it closes above 30.080, the Bollinger uptrend channel could guide the USD toward the top of the channel at 30.250. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.910 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 29.730 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 29.690 (base of Ichimoku Cloud). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.000 (psychological resistance), then at 30.080 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 30.250 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/KRW - consolidation, possible upside bias. USD/KRW opens with a slightly biddish tone as punters position for tonight's U.S. FOMC decision and statement from chairman Bernanke, who may hint again at a tapering of quantitative easing - which would send the dollar higher. USD/KRW is inching higher and into the daily Bollinger uptrend channel that begins at 1,133. A daily close above this mark is a bullish signal that could trigger a rally toward the top of the channel at 1,140. If however Bernanke displays a dovish stance instead, the greenback could sink back down to the 20-day Bollinger mid support at 1,126. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is 1,133 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,130 (psychological support), before 1,126 (20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is at 1,140 (psychological resistance and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,144 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/SGD - consolidation, possible upside bias. USD/SGD may take on a bullish bias if it ends Wednesday above the 1.2635 level that marks the entrance to the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. The uptrend channel could pull the pair up to the 1.2700 psychological barrier, which is also the top of the channel. But tonight's U.S. FOMC outcome will be key to the greenback's next big move. If chairman Bernanke ratchets up the dovish stance as the WSJ's Hilsenrath suggested he might, then the U.S. dollar could retreat much lower toward the Bollinger downtrend channel at 1.2498. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate resistance is at 1.2635 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2700 (psychological resistance and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate support is at 1.2600 (psychological support), then at 1.2566 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 1.2500 (psychological support and daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/MYR - upside bias. The daily chart suggests the USD/MYR pair has more upside potential toward the top of the Bollinger uptrend channel at 3.1700. The recent dollar-buying could be due to concerns about Malaysia's large current account deficit; Prime Minister Najib said Tuesday that he would aim to reduce the gap to 4% of GDP. But the larger theme of the U.S. Federal Reserve pulling back on quantitative easing is the focus on Wednesday as the FOMC meeting concludes. A dovish statement from chairman Bernanke could reverse the dollar's recent rally and drag it down and out of the uptrend channel, which currently supports at 3.1300. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 3.1700 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.1800 (psychological resistance). Immediate support is 3.1500 (psychological support), then at 3.1300 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.1135 (base of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/THB - upside bias. USD/THB is likely to test the 31.00 psychological barrier soon, judging by the bullish engulfing candlestick signal on Tuesday. Traders may be cautiously bullish on the greenback ahead of the FOMC decision tonight, where Fed chairman Bernanke could hint at tapering of quantitative easing. The view that an end to QE will be laid out by Bernanke is likely to drive the pair up toward the weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone at 30.92, and then the 31.00 psychological barrier. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 30.92 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance), then at 31.00 (psychological resistance), before 31.06 (top of weekly Cloud resistance). Immediate support is at 30.50 (psychological support), then at 30.44 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 30.37 (weekly Bollinger mid support).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/PHP -consolidation with upside bias. USD/PHP may stabilize before last week's high of 43.32. Dollar bulls, betting on Fed chairman Bernanke hinting at an end to U.S. quantitative easing, may exercise caution in chasing the greenback much higher from here. The dollar/peso pair is already over-extended beyond the boundary of the upper Bollinger band (standard deviation 2), which implies the market may be slightly overbought. If Bernanke emphasizes a more bearish tone by saying that the Fed will continue to be supportive of the economy by keeping interest rates low, the dollar could recede and head toward the weekly Ichimoku Cloud support at 42.60. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 43.32 (one-year high), before 43.59 (200-week moving average resistance). Immediate support is at 43.00 (psychological support), then at 42.60 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud support), before 42.50 (psychological support).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/IDR - consolidation. USD/IDR will likely be well-capped in the spot market due to persistent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which sent the pair sliding to 9,900 from 9,955 Tuesday. However, the NDF market appears to be pricing in more dollar upside once again as the 1-month NDF contract exchange rate rallied up to 10,210 from 10,025, implying a much larger premium over the spot exchange rate. A higher NDF premium is associated with rupiah depreciation and risk aversion. The 1-month NDF contract, aside from being a speculative \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  derivative, is also used by offshore clients to hedge onshore exposure when liquidity in the onshore market is limited. The 1-month NDF could head higher toward the June 10 high of 10,405 if Fed chairman Bernanke turns out unexpectedly hawkish at tonight's FOMC meeting. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 9,900 (psychological support), then at 9,810 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 9,750 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 9,950 (suspected \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ), before 10,000 (major psychological barrier).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/INR - upside bias. USD/INR may test the record high of 58.98 notched on June 11. Dollar bulls have been pushing the pair up as the U.S. FOMC meeting draws closer; if Federal Reserve chairman hints at tapering quantitative easing soon, the dollar will get a boost and likely break through the psychological barrier at 59.00. But if Bernanke tones down expectations of rising interest rates, there could be a long-USD capitulation that might drag USD/INR down toward the bottom of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel at 57.00. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 58.98 (record high), then at 59.00 (psychological resistance), before 60.00 (major psychological resistance). Immediate support is at 58.50 (psychological support), then at 58.00 (psychological support), before 57.00 (psychological support and bottom of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 18, 2013 20:46 ET (00:46 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130619e96j00044\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
