\par\par \b \uc2 DJ ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,628 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 2013\par 02:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--The following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range Larger Range \f28 \par \par \uc2 USD/CNY 6.1210-6.1300 6.1200-6.1500\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD 29.910-30.000 29.730-30.080 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    USD/KRW  1,125-1,130    1,120-1,132 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/SGD 1.2500-1.2566 1.2495-1.2600\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/MYR 3.1225-3.1500 3.1135-3.1630 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    USD/THB  30.50-30.92    30.37-31.00 \par    USD/PHP  42.60-43.00    42.50-43.59 \par    USD/IDR  9,800-9,890    9,750-9,900 \par    USD/INR  58.00-58.50    57.50-58.98 \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis - Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/CNY - consolidation. A stable WSJ Dollar Index and dollar/yen likely mean the PBOC central parity rate could hover around recent levels. The cash shortage onshore may not have had much impact yet on the spot market but if it worsens, banks might be forced to acquire CNY liquidity via the spot and forward \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, which would have the net effect of sending spot USD/CNY down (though likely to be very limited due to the 1% trading band stipulated) and the forward curve lower as well. The dollar has a technical bearish bias as the USD/CNY pair is back inside the Bollinger downtrend channel, with an eye on the channel base at 6.1018. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.1210 (June 3 record low), then at 6.1200 (psychological support), before 6.1018 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 6.1300 (psychological resistance), then at 6.1500 (psychological resistance), before 6.1699 (top of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/TWD - consolidation. USD/TWD may range within a 29.910-30.080 range, bound by the 20-day Bollinger mid support and the entrance to the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. If USD/TWD ends the day below the 20-day Bollinger mid, the next target could be the Ichimoku Cloud support at 29.730. If the pair closes above 30.080 Tuesday, the Bollinger uptrend channel could guide the USD toward the top of the channel at 30.250. The speculative bets on the outcome of Wednesday's U.S FOMC meeting could be swinging back toward dollar bullishness once again, price action in the G-3 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  suggest. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.910 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 29.730 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 29.690 (base of Ichimoku Cloud). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.000 (psychological resistance), then at 30.080 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 30.250 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/KRW - consolidation. USD/KRW is likely to range within 1,125-1,132 band as it did Monday. There is a risk of an upside move as traders adjust positions ahead of Wednesday's U.S. FOMC decision. Expectations of Federal Reserve chairman Bernanke's stance toward ending QE are slightly more balanced now, after a report Monday said that he would likely indicate the Fed is close to tapering bond purchases, which would be a dollar-positive move. If the USD/KRW ends the day above 1,132, it could target the top of the uptrend channel at 1,139. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,125 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 1,120 (psychological support), before 1,118 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,130 (psychological resistance), then at 1,132 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,139 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/SGD - consolidation. USD/SGD is still caught in a narrowing range of 1.2495-1.2565, reflecting the mixed views of what Federal Reserve chairman Bernanke will say at Wednesday's FOMC meeting. If he hints at a sooner-than-September tapering of bond purchases, the greenback will likely rally across the board and climb into the USD/SGD Bollinger uptrend channel which starts at 1.2636. But if he is more dovish as the WSJ's Jon Hilsenrath suggests he will be, USD/SGD may drop into the downtrend channel and head for the Ichimoku Cloud support at 1.2395. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2500 (psychological support), then at 1.2495 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2425 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2566 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 1.2600 (top of weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and psychological resistance).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/MYR - consolidation with upside bias. USD/MYR may head higher if it maintains its bullish bias within the Bollinger uptrend channel that currently bottoms out at 3.1225. The channel could guide the pair toward the first target of 3.1530 - the top of the weekly Bollinger uptrend channel. The greenback is slightly firmer across the board due to a report that Federal Reserve chairman Bernanke will hint at a tapering of bond purchases at Wednesday's FOMC meeting. The direction of the dollar/ringgit pair will hinge on whether Bernanke puts on a more dovish front as some analysts last week suggested he will. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 3.1500 (psychological resistance), then at 3.1530 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.1630 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate support is 3.1225 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.1135 (base of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.1000 (major psychological support).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/THB - consolidation with upside bias. The dollar's pullback lower appears to have run its course, and the USD/THB pair may now rise again toward the psychological barrier at 31.00. The market is once again adjusting its positioning toward a stronger dollar on a punt that Federal Reserve chairman Bernanke could deliver a surprisingly hawkish message at Wednesday's FOMC meeting. The USD/THB pair will have to first overcome the weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone at 30.92 before it can reach the 31.00 barrier. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 30.92 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance), then at 31.00 (psychological resistance), before 31.06 (top of weekly Cloud resistance). Immediate support is at 30.50 (psychological support), then at 30.37 (weekly Bollinger mid support), before 30.35 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/PHP -consolidation with upside bias. USD/PHP could continue rising within the weekly Bollinger uptrend channel, though the pair looks slightly over-extended on the daily charts. A renewed dollar rally could send the pair back up to last week's high of 43.32; if the greenback ends Tuesday above the psychological barrier of 43.00, the 43.32 target will come into sight. The dollar may rise on shifting expectations of what Federal Reserve chairman Bernanke will say at Wednesday's FOMC meeting. Some analysts are suggesting that he will signal the Fed is ready to taper bond purchases. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 43.00 (psychological resistance), before 43.59 (200-week moving average resistance). Immediate support is at 42.60 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 42.50 (psychological support), before 42.16 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/IDR - consolidation with upside bias. The U.S. dollar is firming up again after an overnight report that Federal Reserve chairman may signal a tapering of bond purchases is coming. Spot USD/IDR is rising toward last week's high of 9,895, a level which will likely trigger the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  into \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  action again to prevent what is deemed as excessive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakness. The 1-month USD/IDR contract exchange rate is rallying again after bouncing off the psychological barrier of 10,000 Monday, suggesting that risk appetite for the rupiah is still fragile. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 9,890 (suspected \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ), before 9,900 (psychological resistance). Immediate support is at 9,800 (psychological support and base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 9,750 (20-day Bollinger mid support).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/INR - upside bias. USD/INR is aiming higher once more, propelled by traders positioning ahead of Wednesday's U.S. Federal Reserve FOMC meeting, where chairman Bernanke could signal a tapering of bond purchases to come soon. USD/INR Monday reversed last week's bearish candlestick formation, and may now head toward a re-test of the record high of 58.98 notched June 11. The street is of two minds now as to whether the Fed will change tack toward being more dovish after the recent routing of emerging markets on the initial hint of a tapering of quantitative easing. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 58.50 (psychological resistance), before 58.98 (record high). Immediate support is at 58.00 (psychological support), then at 57.50 (psychological support), before 57.00 (psychological support).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 17, 2013 20:54 ET (00:54 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130618e96i0003q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
