\par\par \b \uc2 DJ ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,648 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 2013\par 02:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--The following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par            Immediate Range Larger Range \f28 \par \par \uc2 USD/CNY 6.1324-6.1500 6.1210-6.1800\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD 30.080-30.200 30.000-30.250 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    USD/KRW  1,124-1,130    1,120-1,131 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/SGD 1.2496-1.2500 1.2524-1.2567\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/MYR 3.1200-3.1500 3.1140-3.1550 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    USD/THB  30.50-30.94    30.40-31.00 \par    USD/PHP  43.00-43.50    42.60-43.87 \par    USD/IDR  9,800-9,850    9,790-9,900 \par    USD/INR  57.00-58.00    56.56-58.50 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis - Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/CNY -- downside bias. An about-turn in risk sentiment overnight has pushed the U.S. dollar lower and the dollar/yen pair higher, which may imply that the PBOC's central parity rate is going to be stable or possibly slightly higher than Thursday's record low of 6.1612. Spot USD/CNY however, could start to drift back down as investors, calmed by rhetoric that the U.S. Federal Reserve won't raise interest rates just yet, gradually edge back into risk-on short-USD/CNY positions. The overnight rally on Wall Street should support Chinese stocks, which will help to boost the yuan. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.1324 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.1210 (June 3 record low), before 6.1029 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 6.1500 (psychological resistance), then at 6.1800 (top of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/TWD -- consolidation. USD/TWD could slip out of the Bollinger uptrend channel as risk appetite returns, which will likely depress the U.S. dollar in Asia Friday. USD/TWD could hence fall toward the 20-day Bollinger mid at 29.910 where it may then consolidate. An improvement in the U.S. weekly jobless claims Thursday gave the stock market a boost, as did The Wall Street Journal article that suggested the U.S. Federal Reserve will still keep interest rates low even if the pace of bond buying is reduced. Investors may not rush back into risk-on positions immediately, but the long-USD risk-off trades will likely be reduced. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.080 (base of Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.000 (psychological support), before 29.910 (20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.200 (psychological resistance), then at 30.250 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/KRW -- consolidation. USD/KRW gaps lower to 1,126 from its Thursday close of 1,134, nearly reaching the 20-day Bollinger mid support at 1,124 which is likely to hold the pair steady for now. Traders expect a capitulation of long-USD risk off positions to keep a lid on the USD/KRW pair. USD/KRW may turn bearish on a daily close below the 20-day Bollinger mid support. The overnight turn in risk sentiment is pressuring the U.S. dollar lower in Asia and helping stocks to recover strongly; Japan's Nikkei is up 3.5% in early trade. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is 1,124 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 1,120 (psychological support), before 1,117 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,130 (psychological resistance), then at 1,131 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,139 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/SGD -- consolidation with downside bias. USD/SGD may slide back into the daily Bollinger downtrend channel due to the overnight drop in the WSJ Dollar Index, triggered by the better risk sentiment. The pair could soon fall toward the daily Ichimoku Cloud at 1.2395 as long as the top of the downtrend channel at 1.2496 is not breached on a Friday global close. Better-than-expected U.S. weekly jobless claims and a jump in U.S. stocks Thursday are helping to dispel fears of a deeper global risk aversion. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2496 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1.2424 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2400 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2500 (psychological resistance), then at 1.2567 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 1.2600 (top of weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and psychological resistance).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/MYR -- pullback lower. USD/MYR could retreat to the base of the Bollinger uptrend channel at 3.1140 as the greenback takes a beating on improving risk appetite and growing confidence that the U.S. Federal Reserve won't hike rates yet, even if they slow the pace of bond purchases. USD/MYR could break the uptrend spell if it ends the day below 3.1140 and therefore out of the uptrend channel, which could then expose the pair to the 20-day Bollinger mid support at 3.0770. Asia equity markets are likely to see a relief rally--which will help support the ringgit--given dollar/yen's overnight bounce, which is spurring the Nikkei higher Friday. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is 3.1200 (psychological support), then at 3.1140 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.1000 (major psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 3.1500 (psychological resistance), then at 3.1550 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.1600 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/THB -- consolidation lower. An exodus of long-USD positions after the USD/THB pair broke below the 31.00 psychological barrier is pressuring the greenback lower. The abrupt improvement in risk appetite overnight is likely to deter more bullish-USD bets and hence weigh the USD/THB pair toward the base of the Bollinger uptrend channel at 30.32, where it will likely consolidate. Investors are rationalizing that even if the U.S. Federal Reserve slows the pace of bond purchases, interest rates won't rise just yet, given the weak recovery in the U.S. unemployment rate. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.50 (psychological support), then at 30.40 (weekly Bollinger mid support), before 30.32 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 30.94 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance), then at 30.96 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 31.00 (psychological resistance).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/PHP --consolidation lower. USD/PHP is likely to fall back toward the weekly Ichimoku Cloud at 42.60 and then consolidate. The greenback is retreating sharply as risk appetite returns. The market seems to be coming around to the notion that the U.S. Federal Reserve reducing its pace of bond purchases doesn't mean interest rates will be hiked yet. As long as the market believes benchmark U.S. interest rates will continue to be kept low for some time, the greenback will slide back down again. Manila stocks will likely recover strongly from the recent selloff, which will thus help the peso to rebound as well. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.00 (psychological support), then at 42.60 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud support), before 42.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 43.50 (psychological resistance), before 43.87 (monthly Bollinger mid resistance).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/IDR -- consolidation lower. Spot USD/IDR slipped a tad after the Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raised the benchmark interest rate by 25 basis points to 6.0%, which surprised the market. The rupiah only rose mildly on the policy decision Thursday, but it could get a huge boost from the overnight slump of the U.S. dollar as the market readjusts its expectations of what U.S. Federal Reserve chairman Bernanke will say at next week's policy meeting. The WSJ article--that the Fed might keep rates low even if bond buying eases--boosted investor sentiment overnight and is triggering a selloff in long-USD positions. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 9,800 (psychological support), then at 9,790 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 9,750 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 9,850 (suspected \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ), before 9,900 (psychological resistance).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/INR -- downside bias. USD/INR is likely to turn around and slip toward the base of the Bollinger uptrend channel at 56.56, though the 57.00 psychological barrier will likely help prop up the pair in the interim. The chart reversal signal confirmed Wednesday, coupled with the additional long-tailed doji candlestick Thursday, presents a convincing case that the USD/INR pair is overbought and due for a pullback. The overnight fall in the WSJ Dollar Index, due to a change in the way the market perceives the Federal Reserve will act at next week's policy meeting, will help pressure the pair lower. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 57.00 (psychological support), then at 56.56 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 58.00 (psychological resistance), then at 58.50 (psychological resistance), before 58.98 (record high).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\f28 \p