\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,557 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2013\par 03:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--The following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range Larger Range \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 USD/CNY 6.1334-6.1500 6.1210-6.1800\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD 30.070-30.200 30.000-30.230\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    USD/KRW  1,130-1,138   1,123-1,140 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/SGD 1.2533-1.2574 1.2510-1.2600\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/MYR 3.1200-3.1500 3.1140-3.1550\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    USD/THB  30.80-30.94   30.40-31.00 \par    USD/PHP  42.60-43.00   42.50-43.50 \par    USD/IDR  9,800-9,850   9,790-9,900 \par    USD/INR  57.00-58.00   56.50-58.50 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis - Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/CNY -- downside bias. The PBOC's central parity rate is expected to be significantly lower than the last parity rate set on Friday before China markets closed for holidays, due to the sharp drop in dollar/yen since then. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's valuation method for the yuan is influenced by the Japanese yen's value. Dollar/yuan is likely to mark a new record low if the parity rate comes much lower today. However, recently weaker China exports and slowing manufacturing growth data could temper the market's appetite for yuan exposure. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 6.1334 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.1210 (June 3 record low), before 6.1034 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 6.1500 (psychological resistance), then at 6.1800 (top of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/TWD -- consolidation with upside bias. Despite the slippage in the WSJ Dollar Index overnight, USD/TWD could retain its upside bias within the Bollinger uptrend channel as risk aversion continues to grip emerging markets, triggering a flight to the U.S. dollar. However, if the Chinese yuan marks a significantly stronger parity rate, the Taiwan dollar could recover, being a close proxy to the yuan. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taiwan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep the Taiwan dollar from appreciating too much, ostensibly to keep the country's exports competitively priced. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is likely at 30.200 (psychological resistance), then at 30.230 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate support is at 30.070 (base of Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.000 (psychological support), before 29.900 (20-day Bollinger mid).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/KRW -- upside bias. USD/KRW is back inside the daily Bollinger uptrend channel, which will likely guide the pair up to the top of the channel at 1,138. The risk aversion in emerging markets will continue to erode the South Korea won, which has temporarily lost its direct correlation with the Japanese yen. The USD/KRW pair typically moves along with the USD/JPY pair as \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  regularly monitors the relative value of the yen versus the won to maintain a competitive advantage for South Korea exporters. So, if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakens too much on an intraday basis, traders expect \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Korea\f28 \uc2 \f2  to step in to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by selling U.S. dollars in the market to support the won. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 1,138 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,140 (psychological resistance), before 1,145 (2013 high). Immediate support is 1,130 (base of Bollinger uptrend channel and psychological support), then at 1,123 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 1,120 (psychological support).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/SGD -- consolidation. USD/SGD is still in consolidation territory between the Bollinger downtrend channel and the 20-day Bollinger mid resistance line. The pair has been relatively stable due to the Singapore dollar's status as a regional safe-haven \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , making it fairly immune to risk aversion-related selloffs of peer \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . A possible trigger that could ignite a larger move in the USD/SGD pair could be a sharply lower USD/CNY parity rate -- as China's PBOC reacts to the steep drop in USD/JPY since Friday. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2533 (base of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2510 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2500 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2574 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 1.2600 (top of weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and psychological resistance), before 1.2640 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/MYR -- upside bias. The charts suggest USD/MYR may rise toward the top of the Bollinger uptrend channel, driven by persistent risk aversion in emerging markets. The global stock market selloff, which so far has not hurt Malaysia stocks much, is likely to do so soon, which could then trigger more outflows from the ringgit. Though the WSJ Dollar Index is a tad weaker due to the rise of the euro and the fall of dollar/yen, the signs of risk aversion in the bond market reveal that more weakness for emerging market assets could be at hand. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 3.1500 (psychological resistance), then at 3.1550 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.1580 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate support is 3.1200 (psychological support), then at 3.1140 (base of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.1000 (psychological support and base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/THB -- consolidation. USD/THB has dropped back under the weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone of 30.94-31.06 due to profit-taking and will likely consolidate slightly lower for now, said a dealer in Singapore. The pair may retreat toward the psychological support near 30.80 as the market trims its bearish bets on the baht, spooked by the sharp turnaround Wednesday. But if the pair manages to climb past the top of the weekly Cloud by Friday, more upside is likely in the mid-term. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.80 (psychological support), then at 30.40 (weekly Bollinger mid support), before 30.28 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 30.94 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance), then at 31.00 (psychological resistance), before 31.06 (top of weekly Cloud resistance).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/PHP -- upside bias. USD/PHP may be in for a pullback lower toward the weekly Ichimoku Cloud support zone at 42.60 as traders return from Wednesday's holiday and react to the slightly lower WSJ Dollar Index. Though risk aversion and dollar-buying are still the theme in emerging markets, the steep fall in regional leader USD/JPY, and possibly in USD/CNY, could weigh on USD/PHP Thursday. But as long as the USD/PHP pair stays above the weekly Cloud by the end of Friday, the mid-term outlook for the greenback is still for further upside. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 43.00 (psychological resistance), then at 43.50 (psychological resistance), before 43.87 (monthly Bollinger mid resistance). Immediate support is at 42.60 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 42.50 (psychological support), before 42.00 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/IDR -- consolidation. Spot USD/IDR will likely be stable at current elevated levels as the Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been aggressively keeping a lid on the pair, though it has shifted its selling level to around 9,850-9,860 from 9,810-9,820 earlier this week -- which reveals that the BI is gradually allowing the rupiah to depreciate along with regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Traders will be watching for signs of normalization in the 1-month NDF premium -- the price difference over the standard spot contract -- before resuming confidence in the rupiah. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 9,800 (psychological support), then at 9,790 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 9,750 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 9,850 (suspected \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ), before 9,900 (psychological resistance).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/INR -- downside bias. USD/INR may be in for a sharper fall Thursday, judging by the uptrend reversal candlestick pattern formed Wednesday. The pair could fall toward the 57.00 psychological support due to profit-taking amid bullish-rupee calls from analysts suggesting that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Indian government\f28 \uc2 \f2  is making the right moves to correct the current account deficit -- a major bugbear for the rupee. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 57.00 (psychological support), then at 56.50 (psychological support), before 56.30 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 58.00 (psychological resistance), then at 58.50 (psychological resistance), before 58.98 (record high).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.) [ 13-06-13 0104GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1136   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130613e96d0000y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
