\par\par \b \uc2 DJ ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2013\par 02:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--The following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range Larger Range \par    USD/CNY       -              - \f28 \par \par \uc2 USD/TWD 30.050-30.200 30.000-30.220 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    USD/KRW  1,130-1,136    1,128-1,140 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/SGD 1.2571-1.2600 1.2539-1.2633\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/MYR 3.1200-3.1390 3.1130-3.1500 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    USD/THB  30.41-30.94    30.00-31.00 \par    USD/PHP  42.60-43.00   42.50-43.50 \par    USD/IDR  9,770-9,800    9,720-9,820 \par    USD/INR  58.00-58.50    57.51-59.00 \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis - Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/CNY - markets are closed for a holiday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/TWD - upside bias. USD/TWD has an upside bias within the Bollinger uptrend channel which supports the pair at 30.050. The immediate resistance for the USD/TWD pair is the top of the channel at 30.220. The WSJ Dollar Index gained overnight as the U.S. 10-year Treasury yield rose yet again. The greenback's bullishness, particularly against Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , is likely to continue Tuesday. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is likely at 30.200 (psychological resistance), then at 30.220 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate support is at 30.050 (base of Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.000 (psychological support), before 29.890 (20-day Bollinger mid).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/KRW - upside bias. USD/KRW may cross into the daily Bollinger uptrend channel at 1,128 Tuesday, buoyed by the rising WSJ Dollar Index. A daily close within the uptrend channel could take the USD/KRW pair up to 1,136 which is the channel's ceiling. With \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  bond yields higher overnight, traders are turning more bullish on the dollar and are starting to position themselves long dollars instead of just covering their previous shorts. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 1,136 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,140 (psychological resistance). Immediate support is 1,130 (psychological support), then at 1,128 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,120 (20-day Bollinger mid support and psychological support).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/SGD - consolidation with upside bias. USD/SGD has a mild upside bias now that the pair has risen above the 20-day Bollinger mid line. But sustained upside momentum may depend on entry into the Bollinger uptrend channel at 1.2642. The Singapore dollar has been weakening against the greenback, but less so than its South East Asia neighbors, due to the inherent 'safe haven' appeal of the Sing dollar. But the rising U.S. dollar will likely overcome the SGD soon as fundamentals continue to improve for the U.S.; S&P's upgrade of its outlook for the U.S. credit rating to stable from negative will add fuel to the greenback's rally. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate resistance is at 1.2600 (top of weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and psychological resistance), then at 1.2633 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2642 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate support is at 1.2571 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 1.2539 (base of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2500 (psychological support).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/MYR - upside bias. USD/MYR will likely surpass its 2013 high of 3.1390 as the dollar rallies broadly yet again. The pair's next major target could be the top of the weekly Bollinger uptrend channel at 3.1520. The overnight rise of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  bond yields after S&P's credit rating outlook upgrade for the U.S. is fuelling the dollar higher once more. Analysts are also turning slightly bearish on the ringgit after last week's disappointing trade data which showed Malaysia's trade surplus shrinking, which is worrying especially with the country's relatively high debts. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 3.1390 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel and 2013 high), then at 3.1500 (psychological resistance), before 3.1520 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate support is 3.1200 (psychological support), then at 3.1130 (base of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.1000 (psychological support).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/THB - upside bias. USD/THB is likely to continue rising toward 30.94, the weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance. The pair looks bullish, supported by the weekly Bollinger mid line at 30.41 and pulled up by the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. Renewed dollar bullishness is appearing as the U.S. 10-year Treasury yield rises to 2.2% again after S&P upgraded its outlook for the U.S.. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 30.94 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 31.00 (psychological resistance). Immediate support is at 30.41 (weekly Bollinger mid support), then at 30.00 (psychological support and base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/PHP - upside bias. USD/PHP is looking increasingly bullish now that the pair is above its weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone. The pair touched a 2013 high of 42.79 Monday, and could add to those gains Tuesday as the WSJ Dollar Index rises again. The next major target may be the monthly Bollinger mid resistance at 43.87. Dollar-buying is likely to continue as \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  bonds get sold off and yields rally again, thus supporting the greenback. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 43.00 (psychological resistance), then at 43.50 (psychological resistance), before 43.87 (monthly Bollinger mid resistance). Immediate support is at 42.60 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 42.50 (psychological support), before 42.32 (daily upper Bollinger band standard deviation 2).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/IDR - consolidation with upside bias. Spot USD/IDR will be stable due to suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around 9.810, but short-covering continues in the USD/IDR NDF market, which saw the 1-month NDF contract spike to a 4-year high of 10,405. The 1-month NDF premium, the difference in price over a spot contract, has surged to IDR400 in the rush to buy the U.S. dollar in a relatively thin NDF market; the premium typically trades at IDR30-50 in stable markets. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 9,800 (psychological resistance and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 9,810 (suspected \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ), before 9,820 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate support is at 9,770 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 9,740 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 9,720 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/INR - upside bias. USD/INR is in unchartered territory after hitting an all-time high of 58.16 Monday. The next major target could be the 59.00 psychological barrier. Dollar bullishness is unlikely to abate especially after S&P raised its outlook for the U.S. Monday, boosting the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  bond yields. The INR may be under assault due to the sharp rise in the U.S. dollar, India' chronic current account deficit. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 58.50 (psychological resistance), then at 59.00 (major psychological resistance). Immediate support is at 58.00 (psychological support), then at 57.51 (top of monthly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 57.00 (psychological support).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 10, 2013 20:47 ET (00:47 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020130611e96b0001b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
