\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 2013\par 03:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--The following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range Larger Range \par  \par  \par    USD/CNY       -              - \f28 \par \par \uc2 USD/TWD 29.890-30.000 29.710-30.200\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    USD/KRW   1,20-1,128    1,117-1,130 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/SGD 1.2500-1.2560 1.2482-1.2600\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/MYR 3.1000-3.1110 3.0870-3.1200\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    USD/THB  30.41-30.94    30.00-31.00 \par    USD/PHP  42.00-42.20    41.76-42.31 \par    USD/IDR  9,770-9,800    9,720-9,820 \par    USD/INR  57.00-57.00    56.48-57.40 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis - Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/CNY - markets are closed today for a holiday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/TWD - consolidation with upside bias. USD/TWD could rise back above the 20-day Bollinger mid and take on a mild upside bias once more if the pair follows the lead of dollar/yen higher. If USD/TWD ends the way above 30.050, where the Bollinger uptrend channel begins, upside momentum could increase. The rise in the U.S. 10-year Treasury yield, after the slightly better-than-expected U.S. non-farm payrolls report Friday, could mean a stronger greenback this week. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is likely at 30.000 (psychological resistance), then at 30.050 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 30.200 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel and psychological resistance). Immediate support is at 29.890 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 29.760 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 29.710 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/KRW - consolidation with upside bias. USD/KRW gaps up above 1,120 on the back of higher \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  bond yields, which are supportive of the greenback. USD/KRW may be headed for the daily Bollinger uptrend channel at 1,128, which could impart a stronger bullish bias to the pair. The Kospi will be keenly watched for signs of weakness, particularly Samsung shares which fell sharply last week and dragged the index down. Poor China export data and industrial production over the weekend could imply a slightly weaker outlook for South Korea's exporters as well. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 1,128 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,130 (psychological resistance). Immediate support is 1,120 (psychological support), then at 1,117 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 1,111 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/SGD - consolidation. USD/SGD may drift in a range of 1.2482-1.2560, bounded by the Bollinger downtrend channel support and the 20-day Bollinger mid. The pair is rising along with USD/JPY at the moment, but whether or not the pair can break out of this range may depend on how equities perform. After Wall Street's gains Friday, Singapore's STI could rally and help support the Singapore dollar. However, poor exports and industrial production data out of China over the weekend could dampen risk appetite in Asia. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2500 (psychological support), then at 1.2482 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2404 (daily Ichimoku Cloud). Immediate resistance is at 1.2560 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 1.2600 (psychological resistance).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/MYR - upside bias. USD/MYR breaks higher past the psychological resistance at 3.1000 and may soon test the top of the Bollinger uptrend channel at 3.1250. The greenback is rising across the board, led by USD/JPY, after Friday's slightly better-than-expected U.S. non-farm payrolls data. The increase in jobs added led to another selloff in \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  bonds that drove the 10-year Treasury yield up again, boosting the greenback. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 3.1100 (weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.1200 (psychological resistance), before 3.1250 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate support is 3.1000 (psychological support), then at 3.0870 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.0790 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 3.0500 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/THB - upside bias. USD/THB is likely to continue rising toward 30.94, the weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance. The pair looks bullish, supported by the weekly Bollinger mid line at 30.41 and pulled up by the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2 's threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the event of excessive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength may help support USD/THB on dips as investors trim their exposure to the baht. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 30.94 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 31.00 (psychological resistance). Immediate support is at 30.41 (weekly Bollinger mid support), then at 30.00 (psychological support and base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/PHP - upside bias. USD/PHP is likely to follow USD/JPY upward, fuelled by bullish undertones for the dollar. The next target for the USD/PHP pair may be the top of the weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone at 42.60. The market is increasingly leaning toward the possibility that the U.S. Federal Reserve will taper off the pace of its bond purchases soon, which is thus giving the dollar a boost. The U.S. non-farms payroll data on Friday, though not exceptional, gave traders more indication that the labor market is improving and thus less government stimulus may be necessary. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 42.20 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 42.31 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 42.60 (top of weekly Ichimoku Cloud). Immediate support is at 42.00 (psychological support), then at 41.80 (base of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 41.76 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/IDR - consolidation with upside bias. Spot USD/IDR will be stable due to suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around 9.810, but the USD/IDR NDF market is already pricing a stronger dollar. The 1-month NDF contract, the most liquid one, has breached levels above 10,000--not seen since 2009--and could be on the way to the next major psychological resistance at 10,500 next. The greenback is broadly stronger as traders price in the increasing likelihood that the U.S. Federal Reserve may start tapering the pace of its asset purchases, which will undoubtedly push U.S bond yields, and thus the dollar, higher as well. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 9,800 (psychological resistance and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 9,810 (suspected \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ), before 9,820 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate support is at 9,770 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 9,740 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 9,720 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/INR - consolidation with upside bias. USD/INR is likely to maintain its upside bias as the dollar gets a lift from slightly-better-than-expected U.S. non-farm payrolls data Friday. The bullish dollar tone is likely to pull the USD/INR pair even higher past the psychological barrier of 57.00, though the topside could be limited by the top of the monthly Bollinger uptrend channel at 57.40. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 57.33 (June 2012 high), before 57.40 (top of monthly Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate support is at 57.00 (psychological support), then at 56.48 (weekly upper Bollinger band standard deviation 2), before 56.00 (psychological support).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.) [ 10-06-13 0100GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1136   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130610e96a0000b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
