\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,544 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2013\par 02:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--The following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range Larger Range \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 USD/CNY 6.1210-6.1371 6.1061-6.1400\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD 30.000-30.050 29.890-30.200\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    USD/KRW  1,120-1,129    1,116-1,130 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/SGD 1.2500-1.2546 1.2447-1.2600\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/MYR 3.0820-3.0980 3.0790-3.1000\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    USD/THB  30.40-30.50    30.00-30.95 \par    USD/PHP  42.00-42.31    41.80-42.50 \par    USD/IDR  9,760-9,800    9,735-9,820 \par    USD/INR  56.43-57.00    56.00-57.33 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis - Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/CNY - consolidation. There could be a small uptick in Wednesday's dollar/yuan parity rate as the PBOC's valuation method likely correlates well to USD/JPY, which rose overnight above Y100.00. The blip higher in the WSJ Dollar Index and the U.S. 10-year Treasury yield may trigger mild dollar bullishness which will keep spot USD/CNY supported. The mid- to long-term USD/CNY NDF contracts may however trade with a softer tone due to PBOC governor Zhou Xiaochuan saying on Monday that the time is right for interest rate reform - which will speed up the path toward China liberalizing its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as well. The market is still keenly betting on another step toward freeing up the yuan trading regime this year. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate support for USD/CNY is at 6.1210 (June 3 record low), then at 6.1061 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.1045 (bottom of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 6.1371 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.1400 (psychological resistance), before 6.1500 (psychological resistance).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/TWD - consolidation. USD/TWD could drift within a range of 29.890-30.050, bounded by the 20-day Bollinger mid support and the Bollinger uptrend channel. If this range breaks, the USD/TWD pair could see follow-through movement. The greenback is firming up on the back of hawkish talk from U.S. Federal Reserve voting member Esther George, who said that some sectors are overly reliant on cheap money funded by stimulus measures. The U.S. 10-year Treasury yield also rose overnight to 2.15% from about 2.11%, thus supporting the greenback. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.000 (psychological support), before 29.890 (20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.050 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.200 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel and psychological resistance), before 30.330 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/KRW - consolidation. The USD/KRW pair will likely face an uphill task of rallying unless it can close above the 1,129 level today. The pair is likely to be trapped within a 1,120-1,129 range, supported by the daily Ichimoku Cloud and capped by the Bollinger uptrend channel. The greenback is rising slightly at the open due to the overnight bounce in USD/JPY, but it remains to be seen if there is any momentum to this move; USD/JPY is still biased lower on the daily charts. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,120 (daily Ichimoku Cloud and psychological support), then at 1,116 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud). Immediate resistance is at 1,129 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,130 (psychological resistance).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/SGD - downside bias. USD/SGD still looks slightly bearish under the 20-day Bollinger mid at 1.2546, but an overall firmer WSJ Dollar Index overnight could lift the pair up above this key pivot and negate the downside bias. If however, the Bollinger mid resistance holds, the USD/SGD pair could slip toward the daily Bollinger downtrend channel at 1.2447 next. The market will be focusing on Friday's U.S. non-farm payrolls, which could determine how soon the Federal Reserve pulls back from quantitative easing. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2500 (psychological support), before 1.2447 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2546 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 1.2600 (psychological resistance).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/MYR - upside bias. USD/MYR continues to trade with a bullish technical bias on the daily charts, guided higher by the Bollinger uptrend channel and propped up by the Ichimoku Cloud support zone at 3.0790. The greenback is inching back up, helped by hawkish comments from U.S. Federal Reserve board member Esther George, who said that businesses may be addicted to cheap funding. The U.S. 10-year Treasury yield rose on her comments, adding to the supportive-USD tone overnight. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 3.0980 (top of weekly Ichimoku Cloud), then at 3.1000 (major psychological resistance), before 3.1070 (weekly Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate support is 3.0820 (base of weekly Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 3.0790 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 3.0730 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/THB - consolidation with upside bias. USD/THB may stay elevated near the top of the Bollinger uptrend channel with the bounce in the WSJ Dollar Index overnight. Further upside for the pair appears likely, though the pace of the move may be slow, since the pair is already at the upper confines of the Bollinger uptrend channel. The next major target for the USD/THB pair could be the 30.95 weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 30.50 (psychological resistance), before 30.95 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance). Immediate support is at 30.40 (weekly Bollinger mid support), then at 30.00 (psychological support), before 29.95 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/PHP - consolidation with upside bias. USD/PHP remains biased higher along the Bollinger uptrend channel which now supports at 41.65. The pair could next target the major resistance at 42.60 that is the top of the weekly Ichimoku Cloud. The dollar is likely to stay well-bid above the 42.00 psychological mark for now, given the blip up in the WSJ Dollar Index overnight. Dollar bulls were encouraged by comments from U.S. Federal Reserve board member Esther George who reiterated her stand against excessive cheap funding engineered by the Fed's quantitative easing. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 42.31 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 42.50 (psychological resistance), before 42.60 (top of weekly Ichimoku Cloud). Immediate support is at 42.00 (psychological support), then at 41.80 (base of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 41.65 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/IDR - consolidation. USD/IDR is likely to trade with a supportive tone, but may not rise very much in the spot market due to the Indonesia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  keeping a close tab on the rupiah. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  in recent weeks has been suspected of selling dollars in the spot market around 9,800-9,810 to support the rupiah. Traders may instead turn to the unregulated NDF market to express their bullish-USD view. The 1-month NDF premium--the price difference between a spot contract and a 1-month NDF forward contract--should be monitored for a spike which could indicate risk aversion in Indonesia. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 9,760 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 9,735 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 9,800 (psychological resistance), then at 9,810 (suspected \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ), before 9,820 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/INR - consolidation with upside bias. The USD/INR will likely stay well-bid after the rise in the U.S. 10-year Treasury yield, but the upside may be slightly limited for now as the dollar is already near the top of the daily and weekly Bollinger uptrend channels, which suggests that the market is long dollars. A pullback and flushing out of some of the long-USD positions may be necessary to see a bigger rally in USD/INR. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is at 57.00 (psychological resistance), before 57.33 (June 2012 high). Immediate support is at 56.43 (daily and weekly upper Bollinger band standard deviation 2), then at 56.00 (psychological support), before 55.60 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell 