\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK - Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,360 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 01:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE--Following are expected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par            Immediate Range   Larger Range \par  \par    USD/CNY 6.2060-6.2143     6.2000-6.2227 \par    USD/TWD 29.830-29.900     29.540-30.000 \par    USD/KRW  1,100-1,110       1,087-1,112 \par    USD/SGD 1.2400-1.2435     1.2366-1.2500 \par    USD/MYR 3.0860-3.0970     3.0780-3.1070 \par    USD/THB  29.29-29.50       29.04-29.69 \par    USD/PHP  41.00-41.20       40.91-41.26 \par    USD/IDR  9,710-9,745       9,680-9,800 \par    USD/INR       -                 - \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY -- consolidation with downside bias. Traders expect a repeat performance of Tuesday's Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength despite Cyprus concerns, which ought to weigh USD/CNY and USD/CNH lower. Spot USD/CNY appears to be capped by the daily Bollinger downtrend channel at 6.2139 -- a close below this mark signals more weakness to come. The PBOC USD/CNY central parity rate might be set a touch higher following USD/JPY's uptick and the WSJ Dollar Index turning supportive. Stock markets may stabilize after two days of weakness induced by harsh property investment curbs announced for Guangdong province. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for USD/CNY is at 6.2060 (base of Bollinger downtrend channel), before 6.2000 (major psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 6.2143 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.2200 (psychological resistance), before 6.2227 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD -- consolidation with upside bias. USD/TWD has been holding in a bullish pattern within the Bollinger uptrend channel and appears likely to continue the same way as long as the pair holds up above 29.830, which is the base of the uptrend channel. The firm WSJ Dollar Index could help support the pair as well and lend some momentum toward the near-term objective of 30.000 -- a strong psychological barrier above which there could be large stoploss orders lurking. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate resistance is likely at 29.900 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud top and weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.000 (psychological resistance), before 30.120 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate support is at 29.830 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 29.540 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 29.500 (psychological support).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW -- consolidation. USD/KRW opens Wednesday around its previous closing level, ignoring the heightened concerns that North Korea might come through on its threats to attack U.S. soil. The KCNA report late Tuesday, after spot market hours, said that Pyongyang had ordered its artillery troops to position their guns toward the U.S. mainland, Hawaii and Guam and to prepare to attack, triggering a kneejerk reaction slightly higher in USD/KRW in the NDF market, but this was shortlived. USD/KRW is likely to consolidate around the 1,100-1,110 zone for now. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,100 (major psychological support, 20-day Bollinger mid, and base of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,087 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,110 (psychological resistance), then at 1,112 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1,120 (psychological barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD -- downside bias. USD/SGD has fallen well into the daily Bollinger downtrend channel, which now caps the pair at 1.2425, and is pointed lower toward the daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone that begins at 1.2366. The general resilience of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spurred talk of safe haven flows into \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Singapore dollar, which could be a self-reinforcing factor that is helping the SGD to gain despite recent poor exports and industrial output data. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2400 (psychological support), before 1.2366 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2435 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1.2461 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 1.2500 (psychological resistance and daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR -- downside bias. USD/MYR may trade with a bearish bias as the Bollinger downtrend channel, which now caps at 3.0970, points the way lower toward the Ichimoku Cloud support zone at 3.0780. Ringgit strength appears to be stemming from a capitulation of overly-skewed long-USD/MYR positions that had been bets on ringgit depreciation heading into the elections -- which have still not been announced by the government. The dollar-bulls may have trimmed their positions as regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed strength despite Cyprus concerns, thus spooking those who have been expecting the ringgit to weaken. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.0860 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 3.0780 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 3.0580 (base of Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 3.0970 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 3.1000 (major psychological resistance), before 3.1070 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB -- consolidation. USD/THB appears to be consolidating as short-term traders may have conceded that the baht's rapid rise last week was unsustainable. But USD/THB is still biased lower in the mid-term as the pair trends lower within the Bollinger downtrend channel which currently supports at 29.29 and caps at 29.50. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 29.29 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 29.04 (Mar. 20 low), before 29.00 (major psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 29.50 (psychological resistance and top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 29.69 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP -- might dip before continuing higher. USD/PHP skyrocketed Tuesday due to shortage of USD in the funding market, which forced banks to turn to the spot market for USD-funding requirements, which resulted in massive dollar-buying that propelled the pair way past the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone. The pair now appears overextended beyond the upper Bollinger band (standard deviation 2) and could thus stage a short-term pullback before continuing higher into the long Easter weekend. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 41.00 (psychological support), then at 40.91 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 40.77 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 41.20 (psychological resistance), then at 41.26 (3-month high).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR -- downside bias. USD/IDR could fall as markets price in the appointment of the new Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, who supports more aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to defend the rupiah. Agus Martowardojo said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by selling dollars in large amounts, in contrast to its current practice of supporting the ailing rupiah with relatively small manipulations, so as to instill confidence that the BI can and will defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Traders expect the USD/IDR to slide on this change in leadership, as it means that there is little upside in USD/IDR going forward. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 9,710 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 9,700 (psychological support), before 9,680 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support and 20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is at 9,745 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 9,800 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR -- markets are closed for a holiday.\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.) [ 27-03-13 0046GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1136   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130327e93r0000p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
