uters page ABSIRFIX01 (or such \par                                               other page or service as may replace \par                                               any such page for the purposes of \par                                               displaying the USD/IDR reference \par                                               rate) at or around 11:00 a.m. Singapore \par                                               time on the Fixing Date (such date, \par                                               subject to adjustment as described \par                                               below). Fallback Provisions apply \par                                               as per below. \par                                              The "Fixing Date" means the date \par                                               that is five IDR Business Days prior \par                                               to the applicable Interest Payment \par                                               Date or Maturity Date. The Fixing \par                                               Date shall be subject to adjustment \par                                               as follows: if the scheduled date \par                                               of the Fixing Date is not a Relevant \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 05-02-13 0700GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                               Business Day, then the Fixing Date \par                                               will be the first preceding day \par                                               that is a Relevant Business Day. \par                                               "IDR Business Day" means a day (other \par                                               than a Saturday or a Sunday) on \par                                               which banks and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par                                               markets are