\uc2 \f2  and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par                                                markets (such banks, the "Reference \par                                                Banks") as selected by the Calculation \par                                                Agent. \par                                              If five or four quotations are provided \par                                               as requested, the USD/IDR reference \par                                               rate will be the arithmetic mean \par                                               (rounded to the nearest whole Rupiah, \par                                               0.5 being rounded upwards) of the \par                                               remaining three or two such quotations, \par                                               as the case may be, for such rate \par                                               provided by the Reference Banks, \par                                               after disregarding the highest such \par                                               quotation and the lowest such quotation \par                                               (provided that, if two or more such \par                                               quotations are the highest such \par                                               quotations, then only one of such \par                                               quotations shall be disregarded, \par                                               and if one or more such quotations \par                                               are the lowest quotations, then \par                                               only one of such lowest quotations \par                                               will be disregarded). \par                                               If only three or two such quotations \par                                          