\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indonesia c.bank says no plans for new instruments to deal with rupiah\b0\par\par\uc2 349 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Januar 2013\par 09:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  says will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in market where necessary\par \par \uc2 * To maintain rupiah stability with various existing instruments\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments)\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Jan 25 (Reuters) - \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said on Friday it had no plans to introduce new instruments to deal with the decline of the rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and would continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market where necessary.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rupiah has been one of the world's worst performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past year, dragged down in part by concerns over a widening current account deficit. It was trading in late afternoon at around 9,665/85, down on the day, but above lows touched earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 "We try to maintain the stability of the rupiah with various existing instruments. There is no fundamental change of instruments or anything," the deputy governor for monetary policy, Hartadi Sarwono, told reporters.\par \par \uc2 "But we know the problem is a shortage of dollar supplies ... from day to day. I need to reiterate this because our balance of payments is still in surplus overall, which means that the current account deficit could still be covered by the capital account."\par \par \uc2 But the nature of the capital account, in which a major part was from goods and services, meant there was not always enough to cover the shortfall in the trade balance.\par \par \uc2 "Therefore, BI (\uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 ) must from time to time ... venture into the market to reduce the gap between supply and demand," he said.\par \par \uc2 He said he expected the current account deficit to improve and that demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be met by the market.\par \par \uc2 "As usual, we will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We'll see how the numbers are now. If there is a huge need for oil and gas imports, we will increase more there. So there is no instrument that has changed, only the amount and timing."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Adriana Nina Kusuma; Writing by Jonathan Thatcher; Editing by Jacqueline Wong)\par \par \uc2 INDONESIA-RUPIAH/ (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | IF | M | SI | ABX | E | RBN | RNP | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130125e91p000em\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
