\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah down before govt bond auction; Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  subdued\b0\par\par\uc2 892 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2013\par 02:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Indonesia aims to sell $727 mln bonds on Tuesday\par \par \uc2 * Won dips on importers, offshore funds\par \par \uc2 * Philippine peso eases on dlr-short covering\par \par \uc2 (Adds text, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Jan 14 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah slid on Monday on fears of further outflows ahead of a government debt auction, while other emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed as authorities took a breather from repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rupiah's indicative price softened 0.3 percent to 9,660 to the dollar on exchange pages, but its real market price was a weaker 9,880-9,900 quoted against corporate dollar demand, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's debt also fell, with yields on 10-year bonds\par \par \uc2 hitting 5.263 percent, their highest since Dec. 12, and the five-year yield at 4.713 percent, also highest since Jan. 2.\par \par \uc2 The country aims to raise 7 trillion rupiah ($726.52 million) from a bond auction on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "It looks like investors could be more cautious than the recent auctions, on the back of recent weakening of the rupiah," said Gundy Cahyadi, an economist at \uc2 OCBC Bank\uc2  in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah has slid 0.3 percent against the dollar so far this year after being the worst performing emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2012 with a loss of nearly 6 percent, Thomson Reuters' data showed.\par \par \uc2 Worries about the country's current account deficit and inflation, as well as a lack of dollar liquidity, have been putting pressure on the rupiah and curbing foreign investors' appetite for Indonesian assets. [ID:nL4N0AF2TE\par \par \uc2 The future value for the rupiah has plunged in offshore forward markets, indicating a rush by foreigners to hedge their risks.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Agus Martowardojo said he expected the rupiah to weaken this year on a wider current account deficit and uncertain global economic situation, adding its average exchange rate will be at 9,300-9,700.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been spotted selling dollars to support the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. On Monday, it provided dollar liquidity between 9,655 and 9,680, they added.\par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  also expressed determination to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will always ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if rupiah depreciates excessively from its fundamental," Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Darmin Nasution told parliament.\par \par \uc2 Still, some analysts and dealers expect Tuesday's bond auction to attract decent foreign interest, given higher yields.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah rebounded in the forwards market with one-month dollar/rupiah non-deliverable forwards down 0.4 percent to 9,890.\par \par \uc2 "By looking at the correction last week and not much trading volume, it means that there were not a lot of foreign outflows," said Handy Yunianto, debt market analyst at \uc2 Mandiri Sekuritas\uc2  in Jakarta.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors reduced Indonesian bond holdings by 1.29 trillion rupiah in the first four days of last week, but that compared with average daily bond market trading volume of 9.5 trillion rupiah in 2012.\par \par \uc2 "I think demand at the auction tomorrow will be big," said Yuniato, adding the valuation should be "interesting" with the recent correction.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 The won eased on dollar demand from local importers and as some offshore funds booked profits from the South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Investors stayed wary of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities.\par \par \uc2 Still, the won remained in a bullish trend, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 "Investors appeared to still hold dollar-short positions, but they did not cover those positions actively. I don't think they will aggressively unwind those positions unless the won loses its trend," said a foreign bank dealer in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 PHILIPPINE PESO\par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso eased as investors covered dollar-short positions on caution over further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But real money funds and interbank speculators looked for chances to buy the peso on dips, limiting its downside.\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 The Thai baht edged up on stock inflows and exporters but was also called by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  worries.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0700 GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        89.57          89.19       -0.42\par  Sing dlr        1.2266         1.2253       -0.11\par  Taiwan dlr      28.945         29.039       +0.32\par  Korean won     1056.00        1054.70       -0.12\par  Baht             30.26          30.29       +0.10\par  Peso             40.67          40.61       -0.15\par  Rupiah         9660.00        9630.00       -0.31\par  Rupee            54.68          54.76       +0.14\par  Ringgit         3.0165         3.0210       +0.15\par  Yu