\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/IDR Down On Suspected  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 , But Demand Robust\b0\par\par\uc2 183 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2013\par 04:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0321 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/IDR is a tad lower at 9,700, from 9,730 late Thursday in Asia, as \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  is suspected of selling total of $60 million at 9,700 to limit IDR weakness, two dealers say. One of them says that \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also helps lower USD/IDR rates for corporates and individuals, down to 9,850 from 9,875 late Thursday. But dealers note the USD/IDR is still well bid as importers still need dollars. Bank Indonesia Deputy Governor Sarwono said Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will raise interest rates when the rupiah depreciates "excessively for too long," signaling its readiness to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But he adds that he sees no urgency in raising the interest rate at this point in time. Dealers tip a 9,700-9,800 range for the pair today. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 [ 11-01-13 0321GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1012 1085 1848 5055 55109 75112   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130111e91b0003i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
