\par\par \b \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  Will 'Continue to Be in the Market' - Deputy Governor\b0\par\par\uc2 By Farida Husna   \par \uc2 246 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2013\par 09:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA--Bank Indonesia Deputy Gov. Hartadi Sarwono said Thursday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will raise interest rates when the rupiah depreciates "excessively for too long," signaling its readiness to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rupiah was the worst-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia against the U.S. dollar last year, losing over 6% largely due to worries over Indonesia's wide current account deficit. The depreciation trend is likely to continue this year, with the local unit already falling 0.5% in just the first seven working days of this year.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar has breached the psychological resistance of IDR9,800 in recent sessions, but dealers suspect \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the local unit stable. The rupiah was quoted at around IDR9,730 at 0800 GMT Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Still, Mr. Sarwono said that he sees no urgency in raising the interest rate at this point in time. He added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to be in the market to smooth out \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves.\par \par \uc2 He also said that "even when the rupiah hits 9,800, it has no impact to inflation," in a bid to try to ease investors' concerns over the ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its benchmark policy rate steady at 5.75%, in line with expectations.