\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -QE3 pumps flows into Asia; India reforms power rupee\b0\par\par\uc2 1,210 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2012\par 03:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Won at 6-1/2 mth high on stock inflows\par \par \uc2  * Taiwan dlr up on foreign funds, exporters; c.bank caps\par \par \uc2  * Rupiah hits near 7-wk high on bond inflows\par \par \uc2  * Philippine peso ease; negative fwds prompt profit-taking \par \par \uc2 (Adds text, updates prices)\par \par \uc2  By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Sept 17 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  extended gains on Monday, enjoying capital inflows to the region after the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's aggressive policy stimulus last week, and the Indian rupee hit a four-month high on the government's reforms.\par \par \uc2  The rupee has gained up to 1.2 percent to 53.66, the strongest since May 15, as the Indian government on Friday opened up the country's supermarket sector to foreign retailers  and allowed more foreign investment in airlines and broadcasters, a day after sharply increasing the price of heavily-subsidized diesel. \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won hit a six-and-a-half month high on stock inflows, and the Taiwan dollar touched its peak in more than four months on incoming funds.\par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah also hit a near seven-week high on bond inflows.\par \par \uc2  "Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have room to rise further as the Fed did not only pump up money but also let investors buy time," said Jeong My-young, Samsung Futures' research head in Seoul.\par \par \uc2  "Most risk \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially the euro, looked technically overbought. But Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not fall much even though the euro may see corrections, as people will look for chances to buy the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the euro," she added.\par \par \uc2  Before this emerging Asian units had weakened versus the euro because the regional units did not reflect the rise in the euro on worries that a slowing global economy would keep hurting export-oriented Asia.\par \par \uc2  Still, investors grew more cautious over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by local authorities to stem their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains. The central banks of Taiwan and Philippine were spotted buying dollars, dealers said.\par \par \uc2  Most regional units were also seen excessively bought, suggesting they may suffer from short-term corrections.\par \par \uc2  The 14-day relative strength indices (RSI) of U.S. dollar/Singapore dollar, U.S. dollar/Taiwan dollar, dollar/rupee and dollar/baht stayed below the threshold 30, indicating those pairs are in oversold territory.\par \par \uc2  The RSI of dollar/won, dollar/peso and dollar/rupiah stood above the threshold, but not far from that line.\par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso and the Singapore dollar eased.\par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar leaped to 29.198 against the U.S. dollar, its strongest since May 3, on foreign funds inflows and as domestic exporters chased it on expectations of further appreciation.\par \par \uc2  But the central ban was spotted buying U.S. dollars around 29.200 to slow down the local unit's strength, while importers joined the bids, dealers said.\par \par \uc2  RUPIAH\par \par \uc2  The rupiah hit 9,443 to the dollar, the local unit's strongest since Aug. 1 on bond inflows, dealers said.\par \par \uc2  The Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  found a resistance at that level as local banks bought dollars on behalf of their local corporates.\par \par \uc2  Still, the rupiah is expected to rise further on more inflows with the Fed's stimulus, dealers said.\par \par \uc2  "The QE3 will boost inflows and investor confidence in foreign direct investments here," said a Jakarta-based dealer, adding the rupiah may head to 9,400.\par \par \uc2  "The policy would be beneficial for Indonesia as it would strengthen the rupiah without BI having to dig deep into its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves," said the dealer, referring to \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem weakness in the rupiah, according to dealers.\par \par \uc2  WON\par \par \uc2  The won advanced to 1,113.3 per greenback, its strongest since March 2, on demand linked to foreign investors' stock purchases.\par \par \uc2  Foreigners bought a net 503.1 billion won ($450.38 million) worth of Seoul shares after absorbing a net 1.28 trillion won on Friday, according to the Korea Exchange data.\par \par \uc2  Caution grew over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities to stem the won's strength, and domestic importers bought dollars for payments.\par \par \uc2  "The authorities may allow more gains if the euro and stocks stay firm, while the speed of appreciation is slow," said a senior foreign bank dealer in Seoul.\par \par \uc2  "But they will step in 1,110," he said.\par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO\par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso weakened as traders reduced bullish positions with short-term forwards negative and as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying dollars, dealers said.\par \par \uc2  The peso started local trade firm at a session peak of 41.33 per dollar, but turned lower. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen around 41.35, dealers said.\par \par \uc2  "Onshore swap points collapsed and were quoted at negative points. Negative points have a negative carry on long peso positions and make it expensive to hold on to dollar short positions overnight," a foreign bank dealer in Manila.\par \par \uc2  Most of the short-term peso forwards from overnight to two-month were quoted at a discount, indicating that it was costlier to hold a short dollar position.\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar eased on local bank offers around 1.2200 to U.S. dollar with disappointing export data cementing caution over the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Singapore's non-oil exports in August fell more than expected, raising the prospects of the city-state entering into a recession. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \par \par \uc2  Change on the day at 0655 GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        78.27          78.38       +0.14\par  Sing dlr        1.2237         1.2200       -0.30\par  Taiwan dlr      29.276         29.469       +0.66\par  Korean won     1115.77        1117.20       +0.13\par  Baht             30.80          30.74       -0.19\par  Peso             41.56          41.42       -0.34\par  Rupiah         9455.00        9500.00       +0.48\par  Rupee            54.09          54.30       +0.39\par *Ringgit         3.0350         3.0420       +0.23\par  Yuan            6.3156         6.3145       -0.02\par  Change so far in 2012\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        78.27          76.92       -1.73\par  Sing dlr        1.2237         1.2969       +5.98\par  Taiwan dlr      29.276         30.290       +3.46\par  Korean won     1115.77        1151.80    