\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Portfolio Flows,  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Reserves Pressure Bank Indonesia-ANZ\b0\par\par\uc2 201 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2012\par 08:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0602 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia's growing reliance on portfolio flows and the worsening adequacy of its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are setting the stage for \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to tighten financial conditions more quickly and scale back \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts that seek to prop up the rupiah, ANZ writes in a research note. "We think BI should shift its monetary policy to a neutral stance to tighten financial conditions and limit aggregate demand," the house writes, suggesting that a 75bps increase in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deposit facility be completed in the next two months.\par \par \uc2  The house also says the bank's policy goal of maintaining a stable rupiah is becoming less tenable through large-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , "as the country's scheduled external financing requirements are rising relative to \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves." Limiting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would constrain USD-funded onshore credit activity and possibly dampen the onshore credit cycle, but "it would ultimately forestall the risk of potentially bigger market-driven \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  adjustments" that could threaten current growth forcasts, ANZ says. (ben.otto@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 30-08-12 0602GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1012 1085 1848 75112   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120830e88u000al\par