\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Bank Indonesia Deputy Governor: To Keep Supplying Dollars to Prevent Steep Rupiah Fall\b0\par\par\uc2 565 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2012\par 06:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid a foreign selloff of rupiah assets, says bank's deputy governor\par \par \uc2 -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to announce new measures to curb rupiah volatily, bank director says\par \par \uc2 (Adds context throughout, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  update in 5th paragraph, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  director's comments in 7th paragraph.)\par \par \uc2 By Joko Hariyanto\par \par \uc2 Special to Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA--Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to supply the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market with dollars to prevent the rupiah from falling excessively, following its strongest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the year, while new measures to tame the rupiah's volatility could be introduced this week, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials said Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "The weakness of the rupiah and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is because of the worsening situation in Europe, which has spread from Greece to other countries such as Spain," Bank Indonesia Deputy Gov. Hartadi Sarwono told Dow Jones Newswires in a text message.\par \par \uc2 "As long as [Europe's] problems remain unsolved, the dollar will remain strong," he said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been suspected of increasing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since last week, after the rupiah fell to its lowest level since December 2009. Traders said the week's total \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely topped $2 billion, the biggest this year.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday morning, after Mr. Sarwono's comments, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of selling another $70 million to stem the rupiah's slide.\par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia Director of Islamic Banking Edy Setiadi later told reporters in Singapore the bank may announce more measures to deal with the volatility in the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "There will be an announcement from the governor maybe this week," Mr. Setiadi said, adding Indonesia still suffers "from the turbulence from the European countries," so the priority is still there to temper the "volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 A growing current account deficit and a monthlong foreign selloff of rupiah assets have added pressure on the rupiah, Southeast Asia's worst-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2012. The rupiah has fallen more than 4% on the year.\par \par \uc2 Part of the problem recently has been a lack of dollar liquidity, frustrating foreigners rushing to sell rupiah assets and return to safe havens amid the economic uncertainty in Europe.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors, who hold roughly 60% of the local stock market, purchased a net 10 trillion rupiah ($1.1 billion) in stocks in the first quarter of the year but nearly erased those gains in May. A similar selloff occurred amid worries over Greece in the third quarter last year, but the losses proved temporary.\par \par \uc2 To boost dollar liquidity, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said last week it would use its sizeable \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to prop up the rupiah and that it plans to introduce dollar-denominated term deposits within the next two weeks, to persuade banks in the country to keep their U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with Bank Indonesia instead of offshore. This is expected to boost its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to boost its capacity for further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves are relatively high in historical terms, topping $113 billion before the latest round of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week.\par \par \uc2 --Sam Holmes and Ben Otto contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Joko Hariyanto at jokems@gmail.com, Ben Otto at ben.otto@dowjones.com and Sam Holmes in Singapore at sam.holmes@dowjones.com. [ 05-06-12 0434GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120605e86500079\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
