\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/IDR Down; USD Demand Robust, BI Selling Suspected\b0\par\par\uc2 151 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 2012\par 03:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0147 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/IDR is lower at 9,350, from 9,410 late Thursday, on suspected Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Two traders suspect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to have sold $5 million at IDR9,350 to drive the pair lower. But dealers expect the pair to quickly rebound as demand for dollars remain robust while supply is still scanty. "The euro's fall against the dollar may push the USD/IDR higher, to the 9,500 area later today. But Bank Indonesia will likely sell more dollars before the market closes to drive the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair down again," one dealer says. He tips a 9,350-9,550 range for the day. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 [ 01-06-12 0147GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1012 1085 1848 5055 55109 75112   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120601e8610002z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
