\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Spain banks woes hit; rupiah, peso fall\b0\par\par\uc2 1,233 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 2012\par 09:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Month-end corp dlr demand, foreign banks hit rupiah\par \par \uc2 * Philippine peso down on fixing-linked dlr bids, specs\par \par \uc2 * Baht at 4-mth low on gold importers; 31.92/dlr seen supportive\par \par \uc2 * S.Korean exporters relive won\par \par \uc2 (Adds details, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, May 30 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped on Wednesday as investors cut back on risky assets on escalating worries about Spain's banking sector, while Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move to support the ailing rupiah along with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to arrest its slide.\par \par \uc2 Risk worries also restrained the peso's gains after Tuesday's rating outlook upgrade by \uc2 Moody's Investors Service\uc2  as interbank speculators continues to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and on fixing-related dollar demand.\par \par \uc2 "When we have such a strong USD thrust in the market, it is unclear where the bottom (for emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is," said Sacha Tihanyi, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Scotia Capital in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 "Of course the worst case scenario can be compared with 2008-2009. If that is the benchmark then there is much scope yet for depreciation in Asia ex-Japan," Tihanyi added, referring to the period of global financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 A government source told Reuters on Tuesday that Spain would likely recapitalise Bankia, which asked for 19 billion euros on Friday, by issuing new debt and possibly drawing cash from the bank restructuring fund and Treasury reserves.\par \par \uc2 The 10-year Spanish government bond yield hit a six-month high on Tuesday, with the sell-off in the country's debt having driven up their risk premium over safe haven German Bunds to euro-era highs this week.\par \par \uc2 That pushed the euro to a two-year low and dented Asian shares on Wednesday. The Australian dollar fell after weaker-than-expected retail sales.\par \par \uc2 China is seen also taking cautious steps on stimulus to boost the world's second-largest economy.\par \par \uc2 Beijing needs to bolster investment to spur economic growth but it should shun aggressive fiscal stimulus, influential academics said in leading state-backed newspaper.\par \par \uc2 "Path of least resistance for USD/Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  we think is still up given that the risk appetite decline has grown pervasive," said Emmanuel Ng, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 OCBC Bank\uc2  in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 Separately, the bank said in a note: "Alarm towards EM markets continues to mount with risk premiums blowing out and (we) expect potential USD strength to remain very much a dominant feature in the near-term."\par \par \uc2 RUPIAH\par \par \uc2 Dollar/rupiah leapt on month-end demand from Indonesian corporations and foreign banks' dollar bids, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The pair's indicative price rose 1.8 percent to 9,550, but market prices were higher with some quotes above 9,600, according to dealers.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been spotted selling the pair from 9,420 to 9,580 to select banks, dealers said. Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may calm the rupiah market, some dealers said.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeps supplying USD and it is estimated to inject $500 million-$600 million a day recently. Quite a bit of the USD demand has been met by now," said a Jakarta-based dealer.\par \par \uc2 "Demand by foreign banks is still there but it is slowing down a bit," the dealer added.\par \par \uc2 But investors did not expect an immediate remedy for the rupiah from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plan of dollar term deposits in short term.\par \par \uc2 Another trader in Jakarta said rates offered for the deposits must be higher than market rates to be effective.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Bank Indonesia said the rates will be as competitive as market rates.\par \par \uc2 PHILIPPINE PESO\par \par \uc2 Dollar/peso rose on fixing-related demand from foreign banks and as interbank speculators bought the pair, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the pair slid to as low as 43.205 on stop-loss selling after \uc2 Moody's\uc2  upgraded Philippine sovereign rating outlook.\par \par \uc2 "The 43.205 was a bit excessive with global worries still present," said a European bank dealer in Manila.\par \par \uc2 The dealer expected dollar/peso to move between 43.300 and 43.500.\par \par \uc2 The pair is seen having technical resistance at 43.475, the tenkan line, as it ended below the line on Monday. Dollar/peso had been closing local trade above that since May 9.\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 Dollar/baht hit its highest in more than four months on demand from gold related investors and interbank players, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The pair rose to 31.815, the highest since Jan. 18. The pair may rise further, probably to 31.920, the high of Jan. 16, as worries about Spain's borrowing costs are likely to keep denting risk appetite.\par \par \uc2 But that level may be a strong technical resistance, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 If the resistance is cleared, dollar/baht may head to 32.11, the 38.2 percent Fibonacci retracement of its 2009-2010 slide.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 Dollar/won rose on persistent worries about the Spanish banking sector, but South Korean exporters limited its upside.\par \par \uc2 Exporters' dollar sales for month-end settlements prevented offshore funds and local interbank players from chasing up the pair.\par \par \uc2 "Despite a weaker euro and sluggish stocks, it is difficult to expect a big jump," said a senior foreign bank dealer in Seoul\par \par \uc2 He added exporters will be more aggressive above 1,180 and investors need to also be cautious over possible dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities.\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 U.S. dollar/Singapore dollar edged up, but European investors and leveraged funds sold the pair on rallies.\par \par \uc2 Investors stayed also cautious over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore to cap 1.2800.\par \par \uc2 But month-end demand from Singapore corporations and risk aversion continued to support the pair.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0630 GMT \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen        79.44          79.49       +0.06\par  Sing dlr        1.2791         1.2782       -0.07\par  Taiwan dlr      29.697         29.645       -0.18\par  Korean won     1176.71        1174.80       -0.16\par  Baht             31.78          31.71       -0.22\par  Peso             43.45          43.22       -0.53\par  Rupiah         9550.00        9380.00       -1.78\par  Rupee            56.07          55.67       -0.70\par  Ringgit         3.1570         3.1570       +0.00\par  Yuan            6.3543         6.3480       -0.10\par  Change so far in 2012\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        79.44          76.92       -3.17\par  Sing dlr    