\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/IDR Drops; $400M BI  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Suspected -Traders\b0\par\par\uc2 222 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Mai 2012\par 13:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 1103 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/IDR falls to 9,425 from 9,560 late Tuesday as Bank Indonesia is suspected of selling as much as $400 million to prop up the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , two traders say, adding that the first BI action came after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair rose to almost 9,600 in morning trade. "Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  with about the same amount yesterday too, so the market is taking this as a good sign that it will continue to sell in larger amounts," one trader says, adding that it appears the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also now selling throughout the day when usually it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  only in the morning. The trader says BI's announcement Tuesday that it will allow USD term deposits--a move it hopes will restore USD liquidity to the market--is not yet affecting the IDR, as investors are "aware that this could still be two weeks away." He tips a 9,375-9,475 range for Thursday amid continued BI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  One of the traders adds that BI may have sold $600 million on Monday, possibly the largest amount ever. (ben.otto@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 30-05-12 1103GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1012 1085 1848 5055 55109 75112   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120530e85u000ud\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
