\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesian Rupiah Hits 2-Year Low On Hedge-Fund Attack, Euro-Zone Fear\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ben Otto and I Made Sentana   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 580 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2012\par 13:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah fell to its lowest level in two years Friday as short-term hedge funds attacked the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and risk-averse foreign investors continued a month-long selloff in Indonesian stocks and bonds, adding to seasonal demand for dollars.\par \par \uc2 By Friday evening, U.S. dollar had risen to IDR9,350 from IDR9,280 late Thursday, even after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of selling some $200 million to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the largest amount in perhaps two months, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah has been the worst-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Southeast Asia this year, falling 2.6% on the year and 1.2% so far in May.\par \par \uc2 "The rupiah weakening is now due to risk aversion over Greek fears, unlike in the first quarter when the weakness was driven by concerns over Indonesia's widening current account deficit," said Aldian Taloputra, economist at \uc2 Mandiri Sekuritas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Bank Indonesia doesn't seem to want to buck the trend, as the rupiah weakness is due to global factors and isn't the only \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sliding against the dollar," he said, referring to the relatively small amount of dollars the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold recently in the spot market.\par \par \uc2 Two weeks ago, a Bank Indonesia deputy governor said the global forces behind the rupiah's fall meant there was little the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could do to strengthen the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Traders on Friday said short-term hedge funds were making a speculative attack on the rupiah in the offshore-forwards market, which shook a sluggish market ahead of the long U.S. weekend. Thin liquidity exaggerated the effect, sparking a selloff in other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that prompted the central banks of South Korea and India also to defend their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Bank Danamon's chief economist, Anton Gunawan, said problems in Europe have compounded the customary seasonal demand for dollars in May and June, which is due to offshore debt payments, import payments, profit taking in rupiah assets and holidays.\par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  for weeks by selling dollars, but only to select buyers--including some importers and banks with bond-related flows--and in smaller quantities than normal.\par \par \uc2 BI's relatively low level of dollar selling "leads to worries that if people want to buy dollars they won't get any. Consequently there's no credible rate in the spot market that they can use, so people use the NDF price as a reference for the spot transactions," Gunawan said.\par \par \uc2 NDF prices are typically IDR30-IDR50 higher than Bank Indonesia's spot rate, but were up to IDR400 higher on Friday, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Foreigners have been net sellers of almost IDR6 trillion ($648 million) in the local stock market this month--including IDR0.9 trillion on Friday as the market fell 2.1%--after buying a net IDR10 trillion in the first quarter. Foreign holdings make up about 60% of the stock market.\par \par \uc2 Foreigners also have sold off some $450 million in Indonesian sovereign debt in May, effectively cancelling out April's net buys.\par \par \uc2 Saktiandi Supaat, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Maybank in Singapore, predicted investors would return once global pessimism abated, perhaps after Greek elections in mid-June.\par \par \uc2 -By Ben Otto and I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; +62 21 3983 1277; ben.otto@dowjones.com [ 25-05-12 1142GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1188 4250   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120525e85p000ok\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
