\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  Leaves Overnight Benchmark Rate At 5.75%; Could Mark End Of Easing\b0\par\par\uc2 604 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 08:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  keeps benchmark overnight rate at 5.75%\par \par \uc2 -- Decision could mark the end of recent easing campaign for this year\par \par \uc2 -- \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  to control excess liquidity\par \par \uc2 (Recasts 2nd paragraph; adds \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  comments in the 4th and 5th paragraphs, economists' comments in the 3rd, 10th, 11th, and 12th paragraphs, and market reaction in the 13th paragraph.)\par \par \uc2 By Farida Husna and I Made Sentana\par \par \uc2 Of Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--\uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  on Thursday kept its overnight benchmark rate unchanged at 5.75% in anticipation of rising inflationary pressures as the government is seeking to raise subsidized fuel prices next month.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest decision, which came even as annualized inflation unexpectedly slowed to 3.56% in February from 3.65% the month before, could signal the end of \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 's recent easing campaign, at least for this year, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  vowed to "optimize all monetary policies to mitigate the impact of the government's fuel price policy."\par \par \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  economist Wee-Khoon Chong said "\uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  has completed current easing cycle, and it is now in a fairly accommodative stance."\par \par \uc2 After the monthly rate-review meeting, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman Difi Johansyah said \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  will take the steps needed to head off rising inflation in the short term, including by stepping up its monetary \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to control excess liquidity.\par \par \uc2 He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will also continue to ward off a sharp fall in the rupiah by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, and will buy rupiah-denominated government bonds in the event of massive sell-off by foreign investors.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah has been under pressure recently due to persistent demand from importers and outflows from the stock and government bond markets because of concerns \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 's monetary policy may have been too loose after it surprised the market last month with a 25 basis point cut.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the government is seeking approval from parliament to raise subsidized fuel prices by about a third from April in order to prevent its subsidy burden from ballooning due to the recent surge in global oil prices.\par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia Deputy Gov. Hartadi Sarwono reiterated Wednesday that inflation may accelerate to 7% at the end of the year due to the government's fuel policy, overshooting its inflation target of 3.5%-5.5%.\par \par \uc2 Eleven of 13 economist polled by Dow Jones Newswires said they expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the policy rate at an all-time low, after cutting it by a total of 100 basis points in the past five months.\par \par \uc2 "The rupiah will be helped by the decision to keep the BI rate unchanged," said \uc2 Bank Internasional Indonesia\uc2  economist Juniman.\par \par \uc2 He added \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  should raise the rate by 25 basis points each in May and June if the parliament approves the government's plan to raise fuel prices.\par \par \uc2 OCBC economist Gundy Cahyadi said he expects \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  to unwind the series of rate cuts it has made since last year, bringing the BI rate to 6.5% by year-end\par \par \uc2 The rupiah was at IDR9,125 to the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision, little changed from before the announcement of its stance, but still up an intraday low of IDR9,170 due to a suspected \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Meanwhile local stocks were 0.3% higher at 0657 GMT, while government rupiah bonds were generally steady.\par \par \uc2 -By Farida Husna and I Made Sentana; Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 39831277; i-made.sentana@dowjones.com [ 08-03-12 0729GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120308e838000dz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
