\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ \uc2 IMF\uc2 's Zavadjil: Indonesia Planned Fuel Price Hike 'Very Positive' Development\b0\par\par\uc2 329 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 08:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 1 Mar 2012 02:04 EDT *DJ  Zavadjil: \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  Should Be Ready To Tighten Policy To Prevent Any Spillover\par \par \uc2 1 Mar 2012 02:04 EDT *DJ  \uc2 IMF\uc2 's Zavadjil: Fuel Price Hike Could Slow Private Consumption 'A Little'\par \par \uc2 1 Mar 2012 02:04 EDT *DJ  Zavadjil: Don't Think Fuel Price Hike Would Cause Indonesia Economy To Lose Momentum\par \par \uc2 1 Mar 2012 02:04 EDT *DJ  Zavadjil: Fuel Price Hike To Create More Room For Spending On Infrastructure, Social Issues\par \par \uc2 1 Mar 2012 02:04 EDT *DJ  Zavadjil: \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia Currency Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Still Seems Focused On Limiting Volatility\par \par \uc2 1 Mar 2012 02:04 EDT *DJ  IMF Indonesia Representative Milan Zavadjil Spoke To Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 1 Mar 2012 02:43 EDT DJ  IMF's Zavadjil: Indonesia Planned Fuel Price Hike 'Very Positive' Development\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 )--Indonesia's planned increase in subsidised fuel prices is a "very positive" development, but the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should stand ready to tighten monetary policy to prevent any inflationary spillovers, Milan Zavadjil, the International Monetary Fund's senior representative in Jakarta, said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 In an interview, Zavadjil said that while the step could cause a "hiccup" in inflation and damp private consumption "a little," posing some downward risks to growth in the short term, the country has a very strong pipeline of foreign direct investment and domestic projects, and the higher fuel prices shouldn't cause the economy to lose momentum.\par \par \uc2 In the medium term, Zavadjil said the move would free up more fiscal room for spending on infrastructure and social issues.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IMF\uc2  official also said the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy still seemed focused on limiting volatility, despite its more modest presence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market recently.\par \par \uc2 -By Natasha Brereton-Fukui, Dow Jones Newswires, +65-6415-4044, natasha.brereton-fukui@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 01, 2012 02:43 ET (07:43 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120301e83100238\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
