\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  To Keep Rate On Hold For 2012-Mandiri\b0\par\par\uc2 185 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2012\par 06:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0513 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  will likely keep its policy rate at 5.75% when it meets March 8, although inflation eased to 3.56% in February vs 3.65% in January, as inflation will likely pick up with the government seeking to raise subsidized fuel prices probably next month, says \uc2 Mandiri Sekuritas\uc2 's economist Aldian Taloputra. He expects the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the rate unchanged for the year even though he predicts inflation may rise to around 7% this year. \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  will likely only raise interest rates if the USD/IDR spikes to 9,500. "We expect the rupiah will be under selling pressure" due to the expected negative real interest rate, but \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely respond with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market so long as the USD/IDR still below 9,300, he adds. The pair is at 9,100. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 [ 01-03-12 0513GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1012 1085 1848 5055 55109 75112   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120301e8310008s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
