\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Short-covering supports Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , but poised for losing month\b0\par\par\uc2 1,154 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2011\par 06:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Macro names, specs cover short Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions\par \par \uc2  * Indian rupee has slid 6.7 pct during November\par \par \uc2  * Indonesian rupiah down 3.3 pct for the month\par \par \uc2  * Won finds support from Asian c.bank demand to buy bonds \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, updates prices)\par \par \uc2  By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Nov 30 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose slightly on Wednesday on short-covering after European officials agreed to strengthen a bailout fund, but most regional units lost ground during November.\par \par \uc2  The won found support from a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in central Asia, which dealers said had sold about $700 million in dollar/won on Tuesday to buy South Korean bonds. Some Asian central banks have bought bonds in Korea to diversify their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2  Euro zone officials agreed on Tuesday on two ways to leverage the firepower of their bailout fund, the 440-billion-euro European Financial Stability Facility (EFSF), using both an insurance scheme and a co-investment programme. They also agreed to extend further aid payments to Greece and Ireland.   \par \par \uc2  Hopes rose for more involvement from the International Monetary Fund (IMF) after Eurogroup President Jean-Claude Juncker said there was agreement to rapidly explore ways of boosting the IMF's resources through bilateral loans so it can match the leveraged EFSF's capabilities. \par \par \uc2  However, many investors looked to take profits from gains in emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than to add more bets, due to  persistent scepticism about the euro zone's efforts. The caution put pressure on Asian stocks.\par \par \uc2  "People are reducing long dollar/Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as they sense something is cooking in the euro zone," said a senior Asian bank dealer in Kuala Lumpur.\par \par \uc2  "But the market has not gone short yet because once the euro breaks 1.3200, hell will break loose," he added.\par \par \uc2  The euro, as of 0708 GMT, edged down 0.1 percent to $1.3300 for the day.\par \par \uc2  Most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have fallen against the dollar this month, although they found relief from short-covering this week on hopes of progress in tackling the euro zone debt crisis.\par \par \uc2  The Indian rupee , which last week hit a record low, has been the worst performer among the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It has lost 6.7 percent against the dollar in November, according to Thomson Reuters data. \par \par \uc2  If the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintains the loss or falls more, that would be its biggest monthly fall in at least 16 years.\par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah has shed 3.3 percent versus the dollar this month, Thomson Reuters data showed, although dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars.\par \par \uc2  Earlier, Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's governor said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more heavily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and dealers spotted its dollar-selling. \par \par \uc2  Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are expected to stay weak next month, dealers and analysts said.\par \par \uc2  "The EU agreement is definitely a welcome development in terms of EUR. However, it will be unable to lift general sentiment. I would think the minor risk-on sessions present better entries to short Asia ex-Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the short-term," said Andy Ji, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for \uc2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\uc2  in Singapore.\par \par \uc2  "We will have the usual USD strength in December. European bank recapitalization is likely to take two quarters judging by the experience in the last global crisis. While EUR/USD might get stuck in the range on these offsetting forces, these developments are certainly negative for Asia ex-Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2  WON\par \par \uc2  Dollar/won eased on supplies from custodian banks and South Korean exporters for month-end settlements.\par \par \uc2  But the pair recovered most of its earlier slide as importers and some offshore funds bought it, prompting speculators to cover short positions.\par \par \uc2  Investors were keeping an eye on flows linked to a sale of a stake in \uc2 Kumho Petrochemical Co\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  IFR reported on Tuesday an undisclosed vendor has launched a block trade in Kumho to raise up to 418 billion won ($362.1 million). \par \par \uc2  An official at a bookrunner said foreign investors were estimated to have taken around half of the stake, which \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers say may result in dollar offers of about $200 million.\par \par \uc2  RINGGIT\par \par \uc2  Macro names and interbank speculators sold dollar/ringgit , but some players covered short positions with support seen at 3.1600.\par \par \uc2  In the past, when the pair rose above that level, the dollar strengthened further.\par \par \uc2  A Kuala Lumpur-based dealer said market players are reluctant to sell the pair more, given persistent worries about the euro zone.\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \par \uc2  U.S. dollar/Singapore dollar eased on selling from macro accounts and interbank speculators but recovered most of the slide.\par \par \uc2  Investors covered short positions as the pair is seen facing support around 1.2900. \par \par \uc2  BAHT\par \par \uc2  Dollar/baht fell on offshore banks' selling but its slide was limited, tracking other dollar/Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  The \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2 , as many expected, slashed interest rate by 25 basis points (bps) to cope with the floods and said it would ease policy again if the economy does not recover.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \par \par \uc2  Change on the day at 0708 GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        77.90          77.93       +0.04\par  Sing dlr        1.2972         1.2980       +0.06\par  Taiwan dlr      30.317         30.412       +0.31\par  Korean won     1144.50        1145.40       +0.08\par  Baht             31.20          31.27       +0.22\par *Peso             43.64          43.64       +0.00\par  Rupiah         9150.00        9150.00       +0.00\par  Rupee            52.21          52.03       -0.34\par  Ringgit         3.1775         3.1825       +0.16\par  Yuan            6.3714         6.3778       +0.10\par  Change so far in 2011\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        77.90          81.15       +4.17\par  Sing dlr        1.2972         1.2820       -1.17\par  Taiwan dlr      30.317         30.368       +0.17\par  Korean won     1144.50        1134.80       -0.85\par  Baht             31.20          30.14       -3.40\par  Peso             43.64          43.84       +0.46\par  Rupiah         9150.00 