\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Gov: To Boost  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Market\b0\par\par\uc2 578 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2011\par 10:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 -- Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  says it will step up defense of the rupiah.\par \par \uc2 -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fall further to $112 billion from $114 billion at the end of October.\par \par \uc2 -- Bank Indonesia revises down 2012 growth forecast to 6.3% from 6.7%.\par \par \uc2 (recasts the lead, and the 2nd paragraph; adds context in 4th-5th paragraphs, comments from deputy governor in 7th-9th paragraphs; suspected bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 7th paragraph; economists' comments in 6th, 10th, 12th and 13th paragraphs)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Farida Husna \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Wednesday promised to step up \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to prevent the rupiah from falling sharply even as its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves continued to fall in the face of ongoing capital outflows.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia Gov. Darmin Nasution said besides selling more U.S. dollars in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may start to buy rupiah-denominated government bonds from foreign investors using dollars "if necessary."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By paying U.S. dollars instead of rupiah to foreign investors selling their government bond holdings, Bank Indonesia would help reduce demand for the U.S. unit in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, Nasution added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian government's local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bonds were in high demand in the past two years from foreign investors seeking higher yields than those in developed economies. These investors were attracted to Indonesia's stable political situation and robust economic growth, and in July they held as much as 35% of the government's outstanding rupiah bonds.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign investors have since pared their holdings to 29% of the outstanding bonds, but economists warn the proportion is still high. They say it makes the rupiah vulnerable to sudden fund outflows when investors exit risky assets amid continued uncertainty about the European sovereign debt crisis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Daiwa Securities said in a research report Wednesday that the rupiah is more vulnerable to sudden capital outflows than regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , except the Hong Kong and Singapore dollars, as the country's short-term debt is equal to 36% of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dealers suspected Bank Indonesia sold around $200 million of the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at IDR9,190 after Nasution made the comments. The rupiah has lost 3.8% of its value to the dollar so far this month due to resurfacing concerns over the euro-zone debt problems.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Separately Deputy Governor Halim Alamsyah told reporters Bank Indonesia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves have fallen to around $112 billion, but they are still sufficient to cope with capital outflows.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said earlier this month its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves were $114 billion as of Oct. 31., falling from its all-time high of $124.64 billion in August as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tapped the reserves to slow the depreciation of the rupiah.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Capital outflows amounted to $1.6 billion in November," Alamsyah told reporters.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Alamsyah also said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  revised down its forecast for 2012 economic growth to 6.3% from 6.7% previously due to the bleaker global outlook.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The lower growth forecast could prompt Bank Indonesia to keep its monetary stance accommodative to growth next year, economists said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Of America \f28 \uc2 \f2 Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2 's economist Hak Bin Chua said Bank Indonesia will likely cut its benchmark overnight interest rate by 50 basis point in 2012 from 6.0% currently "if growth readings turn down."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Farida Husna; Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 39831277; farida.husna@dowjones.com [ 11-30-11 0412ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020111130e7bu0002l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
