\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For November 30\b0\par\par\uc2 1,510 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2011\par 08:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par R&I PLACES JAPAN SOVEREIGN RATING ON REVIEW FOR DOWNGRADE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese rating firm Rating and Investment Information said Wednesday it has placed Japan's triple-A sovereign rating on review for downgrade, citing uncertainty over when the country will reduce its debts to an acceptable level. (published 0635 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: JAPAN INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT UP 2.4% IN OCT DESPITE THAI FLOODS, EURO CONCERNS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese industrial production rose a stronger than expected 2.4% in October from the previous month, marking the first increase in two months despite the European debt crisis and the effects of the flooding in Thailand. (published 0035 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: BOJ NISHIMURA SAYS EUROPE CRISIS BIGGEST RISK FOR JAPAN OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A Bank of Japan deputy governor said Wednesday the ongoing euro-zone debt crisis is the biggest risk factor for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's baseline scenario that Japan will eventually return to sustainable growth, warning that there is no quick fix to Europe's problems. (published 0600 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: SOUTH KOREA INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT DATA SHOW SIGNS OF SLOWING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's industrial output grew at a faster-than-expected rate in October, but underlying data pointed to slowing momentum for the export-dependent economy as the euro-zone fiscal crisis pushes the global economy closer to a full-blown slump. (published 0142 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA GOVT: NOV 1-23 EXPORTS UP 15.1% FROM A YEAR EARLIER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's exports in the first 23 days of November were up 15.1% from a year earlier, the Ministry of Strategy and Finance said Wednesday. (published 0050 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: INDIA GROWS 6.9% IN JULY-SEPT, SLOWEST IN OVER 2 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indian economy expanded at its slowest pace in more than two years in the July-September quarter, hurt by high local borrowing costs and a deepening euro-zone crisis, sparking growth concerns that could lead to an early change in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's tight monetary stance. (published 0653 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA FINANCE MINISTER: ECONOMY LIKELY TO GROW 7.3% THIS FISCAL YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's government expects the economy to grow 7.3% this fiscal year to March 31, 2012, Finance Minister Pranab Mukherjee said Wednesday. (published 0650 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: THAI OCTOBER EXPORTS DOWN 0.1% ON YEAR; IMPORTS UP 20.6% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following are economic indicators for October released by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  Wednesday. (published 0644 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INDONESIA\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  GOV: TO BOOST \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will increase \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to prevent the rupiah from falling sharply, BI Gov. Darmin Nasution said Wednesday. (published 0408 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIAN BUSINESS INVESTMENT SURGES IN 3Q, TO DRIVE STRONG GDP GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian business investment rocketed higher in the third quarter, with a once-in-a-century mining boom pushing economists to raise their growth forecasts for the country. (published 0457 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HEARD ON THE STREET: SURPLUS PLEDGE HAMPERS AUSTRALIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's budget surplus target is commendable and rare among developed nations. Achieving it, though, will be tough and could hurt parts of the economy already struggling despite the country's mining boom. (published 0650 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: INDONESIA NOVEMBER CPI LIKELY UP 4.20% ON YEAR, 0.33% ON MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's on-year inflation likely slowed a bit in November from October because of a high base of comparison last year, but compared with a month earlier prices rose rather than falling, presenting the nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  a dilemma as it seeks to ease monetary policy in light of a slowing global economy. (published 0420 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: SAMSUNG WINS AUSTRALIAN APPEAL CASE IN APPLE WAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Samsung Electronics Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . won a significant victory Wednesday in its global tablet war with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Apple Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., when a panel of judges overturned a temporary sales ban of its devices in Australia. (published 0433 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: SAMSUNG C&T TO BUY US PARALLEL PETROLEUM IN A DEAL WORTH ALMOST $800 MLN - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Samsung C&T Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the trading and construction arm of South Korean conglomerate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Samsung Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , will buy a 90% stake in U.S.-based \f28 \uc2 \f2 Parallel Petroleum\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a deal worth almost $800 million, a person familiar with the matter said Wednesday. (published 0435 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHANGYOU.COM BUYS 17173.COM FROM SOHU.COM FOR $162.5 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese online game developer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Changyou.com Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . agreed to buy a game information website from parent company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sohu.com Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for $162.5 million, the companies said in a statement Tuesday. (published 0453 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MELCO CROWN TO LIST IN HONG KONG DEC. 7 BY INTRODUCTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nasdaq-listed Melco Crown Entertainment Ltd. said Wednesday it plans to list its shares in Hong Kong by introduction Dec. 7. (published 0043 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AIG CONFIRMS IT WILL FULLY SUBSCRIBE TO PICC RIGHTS ISSUE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 American International Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday it has committed to fully subscribe to \f28 \uc2 \f2 PICC Property & Casualty Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s rights issue. (published 0049 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: HANA FINANCIAL TO CUT \f28 \uc2 \f2 KOREA EXCHANGE BANK\f28 \uc2 \f2  PURCHASE PRICE BY KRW400 BLN -REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hana Financial Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  may cut the price it plans to pay for a 51.02% stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Korea Exchange Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lone Star Funds\f28 \uc2 \f2  by around KRW400 billion from KRW4.41 trillion, a local newspaper reported Wednesday, raising expectations that Hana may be able to complete its year-long attempt to buy its rival. (published 0429 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA REGULATORS RAID GOOGLE'S SEOUL OFFICE - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Korean Fair Trade Commission on Wednesday raided the Seoul office of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Google Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . as investigations into allegations of unfair trade practices in South Korea's mobile search-engine market continue, a person with direct knowledge of the matter said. (published 0554 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ASAHI TO BUY AUSTRALIAN MINERAL WATER CO MOUNTAIN H2O -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asahi Group Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has decided to acquire Australian mineral water company Mountain H2O, a person familiar with the matter said Wednesday. (published 0556 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: TWO BIG CHINESE BANKS NAME NEW TOP OFFICIALS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Two of China's largest banks have nominated new senior executives in moves paving the way for leadership changes amid a reshuffle of senior state financial-sector posts. (published 0309 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OLYMPUS: STILL PREPARING TO SUBMIT EARNINGS BY DEC 14 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Olympus Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday that it still plans to submit its earnings by Dec. 14 so that its shares can avoid getting delisted from the Tokyo Stock Exchange. (published 0525 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW:\f28 \uc2 \f2 MITSUBISHI MOTORS\f28 \uc2 \f2  PRES: AIM FOR 100,000 VEHICLES SALES OF NEW GLOBAL COMPACT MODEL FOR 1ST YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The president of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi Motors Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday that the euro-zone debt crisis and uncertain U.S. economic outlook won't hurt sales of its new global small car model next year, targeting sales of 100,000 vehicles in its first year. (published 0528 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: VOLKSWAGEN CEO: OPTIMISTIC VW BRAND SALES WILL TOP 5M THIS YR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Volkswagen AG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's chief executive said Wednesday that sales of the brand will likely top 5 million units this year, and VW group sales will top 8 million vehicles. (published 0422 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ACER PRESIDENT: ANDROID TO ACCOUNT FOR 80% OF 2012 SMARTPHONE SHIPMENTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Acer Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jim Wong\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday he expects 80% of the smartphones the firm ships next year to run on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Google Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s Android operating system. (published 0413 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PRADA: GROUP CHIEF OPERATING OFFICER \f28 \uc2 \f2 SEBASTIAN SUHL\f28 \uc2 \f2  RESIGNS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Italian luxury goods maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Prada SpA\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday its group chief operating officer, Sebastian Suhl, has resigned to pursue other business opportunities. (published 0112 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JULIUS BAER SEEKS PARTNERS TO EXPLORE CHINESE MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Swiss private bank \f28 \uc2 \f2 Julius Baer Group AG\f28 \uc2 \f2  is seeking partners in China to pursue opportunities in areas such as asset management, as it looks to tap the vast fortunes built up by China's high-net-worth individuals. (published 0517 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY LOWER AS S&P MOVE HITS BANKS; EXPORTERS FALTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were mostly lower Wednesday with financial stocks coming under pressure in many markets after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ratings Services downgraded its ratings for several global banks, while the backdrop of Europe's debt crisis hurt exporters. (published 0454 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: GLENCORE CANCELS PLAN TO BUY PERU COPPER PROJECT STAKE FROM CST MINING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CST Mining Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s plan to sell its stake in the Mina Justa copper project in Peru to Swiss commodities trader \f28 \uc2 \f2 Glencore International PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  has been terminated, the Hong Kong-listed miner said in a statement Wednesday. (published 0536 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TEPCO: MELTED FUEL IN FUKUSHIMA DAIICHI UNIT 1 ERODED CONCRETE BOTTOM OF CONTAINMENT VESSEL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The melted nuclear fuel within the No. 1 unit at the Fukushima Daiichi power plant was of such intensity that it eroded through 2 meters of the 2.6 meter concrete base, plant operator \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tokyo Electric Power Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said in a report issued on Wednesday. (published 0507 GMT) [ 30-11-11 0717GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111130e7bu000dy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
