ROPERTY PRICES NEXT YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China will prevent property prices from falling sharply over the next six months to one year, but the overall direction of property-market regulations won't change, an adviser to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Wednesday. (published 0314 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: INDONESIA NOVEMBER CPI LIKELY UP 4.20% ON YEAR, 0.33% ON MONTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's on-year inflation likely slowed a bit in November from October because of a high base of comparison last year, but compared with a month earlier prices rose rather than falling, presenting the nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  a dilemma as it seeks to ease monetary policy in light of a slowing global economy. (published 0420 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MONEY TALKS: LISTEN TO BOND TRADERS FOR RBA CUES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the event of a full-blown crisis in Europe and the contagion that would result, Australians would need a lot of help from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 --and fixed-income traders are betting on it. (published 0456 GMT) [ 30-11-11 0501GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111130e7bu00092\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
