\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-UPDATE 1-Indonesia cbank says mkt turmoil complicates policy\b0\par\par\uc2 642 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 2011\par 08:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Inflation in 2012 may be lower than 4.7 pct-cbank\par \par \uc2 * Cbank: exposure of Indonesian banks to Europe almost non-existent\par \par \uc2 * Cbank says \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves still adequate to stabilise rupiah\par \par \uc2 * Cbank sees rupiah tending to be stable in 2012\par \par \uc2 (Adds details)\par \par \uc2 By Aditya Suharmoko\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Nov 24 (Reuters) - Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees inflation below 4.7 percent next year, justifying its recent sharp rate cuts, but uncertainties in financial markets make further rate decisions "more complex", a senior Bank Indonesia official said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Indonesian markets have been volatile in recent weeks on investor worries over eurozone debt, though the exposure of Indonesian banks to Europe is almost non-existent, Perry Warjiyo, director of monetary research and policy at the bank, told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 "Volatility is higher because global uncertainties, especially Europe, are higher," said Warjiyo in an interview.\par \par \uc2 "Those are other factors that we have to include when designing our monetary and macroprudential policies. These have become more complex," he said, ahead of BI's board of governors meeting on Dec 8 to review its benchmark overnight rate.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this year was allowing to appreciate to dampen inflation, fell to a 17-month low of 9,215 per U.S. dollar on Thursday as most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  slid after a weak German bond auction signalled wider fears on European debt.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made a surprisingly large 50 basis points rate cut to a record low 6 percent earlier this month to mitigate the impact of a weakening global economy and keep the Group of 20 member on a strong growth path.\par \par \uc2 Some economists see a further 25 basis points rate cut in December, while others have said the November move was too aggressive given Southeast Asia's largest economy has so far shown few signs of weakening.\par \par \uc2 Warjiyo, a candidate for a BI deputy governor post that will be decided on Dec 7, said the 6 percent benchmark rate was still attractive to investors, after inflation in October fell to 4.42 percent, the lowest this year and nearing the floor of BI's 4 to 6 percent end-year target range.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia has been drawing investors in the past two years after the G20 economy showed resilience to the 2008 credit crisis and on prospects of ratings upgrades, but heavy exposure to foreign funds in the bond and stock market is a problem for policymakers worried about outflows hitting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up a weakening rupiah, pushing its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves down to $113.96 billion in October, about $10 billion lower than $124.64 billion in August.\par \par \uc2 Warjiyo said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would tend to be stable in 2012, with a strengthening trend, but not as strong as in the previous year, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sufficient firepower to prop it up.\par \par \uc2 "We're still confident our \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are still adequate as a cushion to face the impact of rising volatility from the global risks," said Warjiyo, 52, who earned his masters and doctorate degrees in international monetary economics from Iowa State University in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 BI Governor Darmin Nasution has said he expects Indonesian to get an investment grade rating by the first quarter of 2012, putting it at par with countries such as Brazil and China, boosting investment flows.\par \par \uc2 Warjiyo said Indonesian banks remained sturdy, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wanted lenders to lower the spread between lending and deposit rates to boost more loans in stimulating the domestic economy.\par \par \uc2 "The big messsage...is to push further measures so that what we have done can be more effective in supporting the real sector."\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Neil Chatterjee and Ramya Venugopal)\par \par \uc2 INDONESIA-ECONOMY/CBANK (INTERVIEW, UPDATE 1)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020111127e7bo0004j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
