\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Most Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  falls as Europe uncertainty lingers\b0\par\par\uc2 476 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 2011\par 09:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Nov 7 (Reuters) - Most emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell on Monday, led by the South Korean won and Indonesia's rupiah as investors remained wary despite Greece forming a new unity government to avoid an imminent debt default.\par \par \uc2 Some Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also pressured in thin trading on Monday as Singapore, Malaysia and India were closed for holidays.\par \par \uc2 Asian shares also struggled and credit markets weakened, with investors shifting their attention to another debt-burdened country, Italy, putting it under pressure to swiftly restore its credibility on financial markets.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah weakened to 8,985 per U.S. dollar as of 07:56 GMT despite Indonesia's gross domestic product grew steady at 6.5 percent in the third quarter in the face of a global economic slowdown.\par \par \uc2 "I see it'll be difficult for the rupiah to strengthen below 8,800. The flow is mainly from the euro zone, and there will be none in the near term," said a foreign bank dealer in Jakarta, adding the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely keep the rupiah below 9,000 per dollar this year.\par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been spotted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the bond and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to stabilise the rupiah, causing Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves falling $540 million in October to $113.96 billion.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the yuan also fell against the dollar, pulling back from a record trading high on Friday during a summit of Group of 20 major industrial and emerging nations, guided by the People's Bank of China, traders said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0756 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2            Latest bid  Previous  Pct Move\par                               day       \par  Japan yen          78.17       78.23     0.08\par  Taiwan dlr         30.0940     30.025    -0.23\par  Korean won         1119.10     1110.70   -0.75\par  Baht               30.69       30.65     -0.13\par  Rupiah             8985.0      8945.0    -0.45\par  Yuan               6.3473      6.34      -0.13\par                                                  \par  Change on year                                    \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2            Latest bid  End prev  Pct Move\par                               year      \par  Japan yen          78.1700        81.15  3.81\par  Taiwan dlr         30.094        30.368  0.91\par  Korean won         1119.10       1134.8  1.40\par  Baht               30.69          30.14  -1.79\par  Rupiah             8985.00         9005  0.22\par  Yuan               6.3473        6.5897  3.82\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Aditya Suharmoko; Editing by Ramya Venugopal)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For the new Reuters scrolling global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  service please click\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Double click on brackets for following items: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2      Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Asia \tab \par Malaysian ringgit   Indonesian rupiah  \tab \par Singapore dollar    Thai baht          \tab \par Taiwan dollar       Hong Kong dollar   \tab \par Philippine peso      Korean won    