\par\par \b \uc2 Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  Official Hints Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  To Curb Rupiah Decline\b0\par\par\uc2 222 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 November 2011\par 06:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--The Indonesian rupiah's recent decline against the greenback is due to renewed global worries and not the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fundamentals, an official at the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Along with other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region, the rupiah has been losing ground in recent days against the dollar amid risk aversion stemming from concerns over European debts.\par \par \uc2 "There's no [fundamental] reason for the rupiah to depreciate. This is due to sentiment and is temporary. But Bank Indonesia still needs to be in the market," Darsono, an official at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary research department, told reporters.\par \par \uc2 His comments hinted at market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but he didn't provide further details.\par \par \uc2 Dealers suspect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of selling around $30 million at IDR8,995 earlier Thursday, to prevent the U.S. dollar-rupiah pair from breaching the psychologically important 9,000 level. At midday, the dollar was higher at IDR8,990, compared with IDR8,960 late in Asian trade Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah will "remain solid in the longer term" and the country's fiscal situation is also healthy, Darsono, who only uses one name, said.\par \par \uc2 -By Farida Husna, Dow Jones Newswires; 62 21 39831277; farida.husna@dowjones.com [ 03-11-11 0618GMT ]\par \par