\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For October 20\b0\par\par\uc2 2,358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Oktober 2011\par 09:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ SHIRAKAWA: BANK STANDS READY TO TAKE APPROPRIATE ACTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa reiterated Thursday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stands ready to take further monetary policy steps if the economy deteriorates, while committing to keep a virtually zero interest rate policy until price stability is in sight. (published 0039 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: SOME JAPAN REGIONS FEEL IMPACT OF SLOWING OVERSEAS ECON \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Five of nine regions in Japan upgraded their assessments of local economic conditions in October compared with three months earlier, although impact of slowing overseas economies has already been felt in some areas, a quarterly report released by the Bank of Japan showed Thursday. (published 0645 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC OFFICIAL: STABILIZING PRICES STILL TOP MACRO-CONTROL GOAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stabilizing prices will remain China's top priority in guiding the macroeconomy, as the inflation rate is still high though price increases have slowed, People's Bank of China Assistant Gov. Jin Qi said in a speech posted on the PBOC's website Thursday. (published 0231 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PBOC CUTS BOND YIELD, FINE-TUNES MONETARY CONDITIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lowered the yield on a benchmark bond in its regular open market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Thursday for the first time since mid-August, sending a signal that Beijing has started easing monetary conditions to bolster a slowing economy. (published 0439 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par S KOREA PRIME MINISTER: AIM TO KEEP 2011 INFLATION AS CLOSE TO 4% AS POSSIBLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Prime Minister Kim Hwang-sik Thursday said the government will do its best to keep 2011 inflation as close to its 4.0% target as possible, suggesting local officials expect inflation to come in above that level. (published 0208 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: S KOREA REPEATS VOW TO CURB \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VOLATILITY; CONFIRMS MARKET \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean Finance Minister Bahk Jae-wan on Thursday reiterated that the government will act to curb excessive exchange-rate volatility when necessary, and acknowledged that the local authorities \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market recently when the U.S. dollar rose above KRW1,200. (published 0331 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA TREASURY HEAD WARNS EU FAILURE WOULD ADD TO ECONOMIC RISKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian Treasury Secretary and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  board member Martin Parkinson said Thursday failure of euro-zone policy makers to resolve the region's sovereign debt crisis would add significantly to risks faced by the Australian economy. (published 0339 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: THAI SPECIAL POLICY MEETING POSSIBLE IF EASING IS NEEDED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Monetary Policy Committee is ready to hold a special meeting should the economy be in urgent need of monetary easing, as the country is experiencing the worst floods in decades, Gov. Prasarn Trairatvorakul said Thursday. (published 0608 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: VIETNAM 2011 GDP LIKELY 6% - PRIME MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's gross domestic product growth is expected to slow to 6% this year as the country focuses on taming inflation, Prime Minister Nguyen Tan Dung said Thursday. (published 0602 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: INDONESIA 3Q DOMESTIC, FOREIGN INVESTMENT UP 15.3% ON YEAR AT IDR65.4 TLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's official investment board said Thursday domestic and foreign companies spent IDR65.4 trillion on projects in Indonesia in the third quarter, or 15.3% more than in the same period a year earlier, despite mounting concerns about the health of the global economy. (published 0454 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK INDONESIA OFFICIAL: COMMITTED TO 'STAYING IN THE MARKET' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is committed to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to help stabilize the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and financial markets, a central banker wrote in an article published in the Jakarta Post Thursday. (published 0045 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PHILIPPINE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SAYS POLICY STANCE APPROPRIATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will likely leave its monetary policy unchanged when it meets later today, with its governor noting that the current stance is appropriate to help spur economic activity amid global uncertainty and easing inflation worries. (published 0359 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA APPROVES BAOSTEEL TO SELL CNY6.5 BLN DIM SUM BONDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's top economic planning agency Thursday approved state-owned steel maker Baosteel Group Corp.'s plan to sell CNY6.5 billion of yuan-denominated bonds in Hong Kong, which will be the largest so-called dim sum bond issuance so far with the exception of offerings from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0551 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ WATCH: WEAK CPI GROWTH FORECAST SIGNALS NO TIGHTENING UNTIL SPRING 2014 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan may stick to its ultra-easy monetary policy for as long as until the spring of 2014, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is expected to soon release a forecast indicating that the economy will remain in deflation for the next two years. (published 0558 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: HONG KONG INFLATION LIKELY EDGED HIGHER IN SEPTEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's consumer price inflation likely edged higher in September due to a steeper hike in private rentals amid a buoyant property market and a rise in food prices, economists said, adding that prices will likely peak in early 2012. (published 0438 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ 2ND UPDATE: ALIBABA CHAIRMAN: SEEKING PARTNERS FOR YAHOO BID \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Jack Ma\f28 \uc2 \f2 , chief executive of Chinese Internet company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alibaba Group Holding Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., is looking for partners in the U.S. and hopes to meet with private-equity companies in the coming weeks about a potential bid to buy \f28 \uc2 \f2 Yahoo Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., he said Thursday. (published 0426 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA'S ASIC RELEASES CONSULTATION PAPER ON MARKET RULES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's securities regulator said Thursday it plans to mandate exchanges to create a way to stop suspicious trading through a "kill switch," one of a number of measures designed to prevent a flash crash here as regulators contend with the growth of algorithmic trading. (published 0347 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: MICROSOFT COUNTS ON NOKIA SMARTPHONES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Microsoft Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is counting on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nokia Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s rollout of new smartphones next week to give its mobile software a "huge lift," the company's phone chief said Thursday. (published 0628 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA PENSION FUND ADDS 16 STOCK-TRADING ACCOUNTS IN SEPTEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's national pension fund opened 16 accounts for stock trading last month, official data showed, suggesting it is joining the domestic investment arm of China's sovereign wealth fund in buying shares to prop up the country' stock markets. (published 0234 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WYNN MACAU THIRD-QUARTER NET JUMPS 84% TO $209.9 MLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wynn Macau Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Thursday reported a 84% jump in third-quarter net profit from a year earlier as gambling revenue in the Chinese territory continued to skyrocket despite intensifying concern that China's tightening policies will cool growth. (published 2356 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LARGE PACKET OF SHARES TRADED IN PREMIER INVESTMENTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An investor bought 3% of shares in Australian retail group \f28 \uc2 \f2 Premier Investments Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . in a single trade Thursday, according to exchange records. (published 0209 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: WESFARMERS WARNS CONSUMER SENTIMENT REMAINS SUBDUED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Consumer sentiment in Australia remained subdued in the face of higher cost of living pressures, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wesfarmers Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday as it announced retail sales rose 6.5% on the year in the first quarter of fiscal 2012. (published 0324 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GALAXY ENTERTAINMENT 3Q ADJUSTED EBITDA NEARLY TRIPLES TO HK$1.8 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Macau casino operator \f28 \uc2 \f2 Galaxy Entertainment Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday its third-quarter adjusted earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization nearly tripled from a year earlier, driven by its massive new casino resort and soaring gambling revenue growth in the Chinese territory. (published 0518 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SANTOS 3Q REVENUE UP 27%, GLADSTONE LNG ON TRACK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Santos Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Thursday reported a 27% jump in third quarter revenue on year as a slight decrease in production was offset by higher oil and gas prices. (published 2307 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PEABODY, ARCELOR EXTEND THEIR OFFER FOR MACARTHUR COAL TO NOV 11 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The world's largest private coal miner and steelmaker by output, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Peabody Energy Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 ArcelorMittal\f28 \uc2 \f2 , will extend their offer for Australian miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 Macarthur Coal Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . by a further two weeks, the suitors said Thursday. (published 2252 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PETROCHINA: NET REFINING LOSS THIS YEAR ESTIMATED AT CNY50 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PetroChina Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . expects a net refining loss of CNY50 billion this year compared with a profit of CNY7.85 billion in 2010 due to government-mandated fuel pricing. (published 0648 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: NEWCREST MINING OUTPUT DOWN 16%, MARGIN RISES ON GOLD PRICE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The world's fifth-largest gold miner by output, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Newcrest Mining Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., said Thursday that gold output fell 16% in its first quarter to 587,296 troy ounces and costs rose after shutdowns at three of its largest mines. (published 0207 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LEIGHTON DISPUTES S&P RATING DOWNGRADE TO BBB-/A-3 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  decision this week to downgrade the credit rating of Australian construction group \f28 \uc2 \f2 Leighton Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to BBB-/A-3 doesn't reflect the company's true credit quality, Leighton said Thursday. (published 2318 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LEIGHTON, GAMMON JV AWARDED A$1.2 BILLION HONG KONG RAIL CONTRACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Leighton Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday its joint venture with Gammon has been awarded a A$1.2 billion contract from Hong Kong's \f28 \uc2 \f2 MTR Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to build the West Kowloon Terminus Station North. (published 0430 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PANASONIC MULLS RESTRUCTURING TV PANEL PRODUCTION-SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Panasonic Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is considering selling a factory in Japan that makes liquid crystal display panels for televisions, and the scaling down of plasma television panel output at another Japanese plant, according to people familiar with the matter. (published 0338 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASUSTEK CHAIRMAN: EXPECTS TO LAUNCH TABLET WITH ICE CREAM SANDWICH PLATFORM BY YEAR'S END \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 20-10-11 0714GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asustek Computer Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . expects to launch a new tablet adopting \f28 \uc2 \f2 Google Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s latest Ice Cream Sandwich platform by the end of this year, Chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jonney Shih\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 0358 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ORIENT OVERSEAS 3RD-QUARTER REVENUE DOWN 8% AT US$1.44 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Container shipper Orient Overseas Ltd. said Thursday its third-quarter revenue fell 8% from a year earlier, partly because of falling freight rates due to softening demand for international trade. (published 0039 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 THAI AIRWAYS\f28 \uc2 \f2  PRESIDENT: PLAN TO RAISE FLEET SIZE OF THAI SMILE UNIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thai Airways International PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday it intends to increase the fleet size of its Thai Smile subsidiary from the 11 aircraft currently planned, after the unit commences \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in July next year. (published 0406 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LG DISPLAY SWINGS TO 3Q NET LOSS ON WEAK TV DEMAND, ONE-OFF LOSSES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LG Display Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday that it swung to a third-quarter net loss from the year-earlier period due to slumping demand for flat-screen televisions in the wake of a global economic slowdown, which resulted in a decline in panel prices. (published 0626 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SIAM CEMENT: FLOODS TO AFFECT BUILDING-MATERIAL SALES VOLUME IN 4Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Siam Cement PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Thailand's largest industrial conglomerate by sales, expects the sales volume of its building material products in the fourth quarter to be hurt by the severe flooding across the country, company President and Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kan Trakulhoon\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday. (published 0654 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: HYUNDAI EYES 2012 I30 SALES OF 215,000; EUROPE KEY MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is looking to sell 215,000 units of the latest version of its i30 hatchback next year as part of its push to secure a bigger share of premium sub-compact car market, the company said Thursday. (published 0355 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: BIG C SUPERCENTER PLANS TO RAISE UP TO THB25 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Big C Supercenter PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2 's board has approved a planned capital increase raising as much as THB25 billion that will see as many as 350 million new shares offered to existing shareholders, it said Thursday. (published 0449 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AMCOR SAYS FY12 EARNINGS EXPECTED SUBSTANTIALLY HIGHER THAN FY11 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Packaging manufacturer Amcor Ltd. is on track for a substantial increase in earnings this fiscal year, with the benefits of recent acquisitions exceeding expectations, Chief Executive and Managing Director Ken MacKenzie said Thursday. (published 0525 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BHARTI ENTERPRISES\f28 \uc2 \f2 , SOFTBANK FORM MOBILE INTERNET JOINT VENTURE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bharti Enterprises Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the parent of India's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bharti Airtel Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Softbank Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Thursday said they have formally launched an equal joint venture to focus on mobile internet in India, the world's second largest mobile market. (published 0624 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 BIOCON\f28 \uc2 \f2  2Q NET PROFIT SLIPS 3.9% TO INR857 MLN, BUT BEATS VIEW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Biocon Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., India's largest biotechnology company by revenue, has beaten analysts' expectations with just a 3.9% drop in second-quarter consolidated net profit as sales growth strengthened. (published 0536 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 KRUNG THAI BANK\f28 \uc2 \f2  3Q NET PROFIT UP 10% ON YEAR TO THB5.49 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Krung Thai Bank PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday its third-quarter net profit rose 10% from a year earlier due mainly to higher net interest income. (published 0542 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES DROP ON EUROPE'S DEBT MESS; EXPORTERS, EURO FALL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets fell Thursday as concerns over Europe's ability to come up with a credible fix to the euro-zone debt crisis shook confidence, with the Sydney market slipping to a two-week low. (published 0435 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: PETROCHINA: NET REFINING LOSS THIS YEAR ESTIMATED AT CNY50 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PetroChina Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . expects a net refining loss of CNY50 billion this year compared with a profit of CNY7.85 billion in 2010 due to government-mandated fuel pricing. (published 0648 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA SPOT STEEL PRICES FALL; STEELMAKERS' OUTPUT CUTS MAY STEM DECLINE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese spot steel prices have continued to decline this week on the back of product price cuts among key producers, local databases showed Thursday. (published 0517 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIAN CARBON TAX NOT TOO BURDENSOME ON ENERGY BILLS - ORIGIN CEO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's carbon tax won't have a significant impact on the country's household electricity prices, which will remain competitive with those in other developed countries, the head of Australia's biggest energy retailer, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Origin Energy Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., said Thursday. (published 0543 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI RICE PRICES MAY RISE TO $700/TON, FOB, ON TIGHT SUPPLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's rice prices may rise above $700/ton in the next few months due to tightening supply, a senior industry executive said Thursday. (published 0137 GMT) [ 20-10-11 0714GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111020e7ak000j3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
