\par\par \b \uc2 Bank Indonesia Committed To 'Staying In The Market' - Official\b0\par\par\uc2 203 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Oktober 2011\par 02:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA (Dow Jones)--Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is committed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help stabilize the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and financial markets, a central banker wrote in an article published in the Jakarta Post Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "It is with this strong commitment to staying in the market that Bank Indonesia is confident that the policy rate will not undermine the integrity of the domestic financial markets," Perry Warjiyo, director of economic research and monetary policy at Bank Indonesia, said.\par \par \uc2 His comments follow the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision last week to cut its policy rate by 25 basis points to 6.5%.\par \par \uc2 Even after the rate cut, Indonesia's interest rate is attractive for foreign investors, as the differential between the domestic interest rate and that of other Asian countries is still large, Warjiyo added.\par \par \uc2 "Anticipating the impact of the global economic slowdown, sooner or later there will be an emerging downward trend of interest rates across the region," he said.\par \par \uc2 Under such situation, "long-term and rational investors will continue to stay and provide support to the Indonesian economy," the central banker wrote.\par \par \uc2 -By I Made Sentana, Dow Jones Newswires; +62 21-39831277 [ 20-10-11 0045GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020111020e7ak0000k\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cel